":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/experiment_plan.yaml","content":"  deps: []\n- id: plan_016\n  name: Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\n  claim:\n  - C6\n  description: 'D038: 008e_v3 collapse rate 1/2 based on 2 independent seeds. Additional\n    seeds to narrow true collapse probability. If 2/4 collapse → ~50% rate confirmed,\n    same as dt=2. If 1/4 or 3/4 → rate differs.'\n  priority: P1\n  gpu_budget_hours: 10\n  deps: []\n- id: plan_017\n  name: 'CANCELLED — Walker Walk trained dt_emb + subsample OFF (duplicate of 008a)'\n  claim:\n  - C2\n  description: 'D044 CANCELLED: 008a 配置验证确认 plan_017 与 008a 完全重复（trained dt_emb\n    + subsample OFF + H=15 + seed 1）。008a 的\"untrained\"含义是 trained dt_emb unexposed\n    to dt>1 data due to subsample OFF，不是 frozen/absent。2×2 矩阵已由 008a/008d/008f/015b\n    闭合。'\n  priority: CANCELLED\n  gpu_budget_hours: 0\n  deps: []\n- id: plan_060\n  name: Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot (Walker Walk, 1 seed)\n  claim:\n  - C6\n  description: Monitor RSSM prediction uncertainty during imagination rollout; truncate\n    when exceeding threshold. Pilot feasibility test on Walker Walk with dt=2 + subsample\n    ON. If successful, extends to multi-seed + cross-environment.\n  priority: P1\n  gpu_budget_hours: 5\n  deps: []\n- id: plan_040\n  name: Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\n  claim:\n  - C1\n  - C2\n  description: Third DMC environment for stronger generalization claim\n  priority: P2\n  gpu_budget_hours: 45\n  deps:\n  - plan_020\n","numLines":43,"startLine":300,"totalLines":342}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Ui1Ab2GzQ4JjESbqLBLJ6A","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All planned experiments identified. Now generating the best-tier predictions with full rationale for each.\n\n```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 framing 完全成立。论文以 \"Diagnostic Analysis of Value Overestimation from Temporal\n  Abstraction in DreamerV3\" 被接受为高质量诊断论文。三重贡献被认可：\n  (1) CIVO 因果链 (trained dt_emb → RSSM fidelity gap → value overestimation → actor exploitation)\n  配合 NVE≥1.5× 诊断标记 (AUROC 0.969)；\n  (2) MPC vs imagination 架构边界 — TAWM 在 MPC 成功但 dt-conditioning 在 imagination-based AC\n  失败，定位 critic bootstrapping 为特定脆弱点（genuinely novel）；\n  (3) Intervention Hierarchy — 17 seeds × 7 methods × 3 levels 系统性评估，证明 CIVO 在\n  gradient/output/representation 三层均难可靠缓解（首次系统性评估）。\n  梯度大小 ≠ 因果重要性（reward 38-49% 梯度但 reward-only SGS 失败最惨；obs-decoder 16-22%\n  但因果关键）被视为超越本文的可迁移方法论洞察。\n  Countermeasures 讨论成功 preempt R9（Double Q 需重构 255-bin categorical critic；MBPO\n  truncation 无法解决 single-step reward bias；ensemble critics 定位为最有前景 future work）。\n  NVE 诊断 AUROC=0.969 配合 Youden-optimal 独立收敛至 1.53× 的说明，化解 in-sample 质疑。\n  Pixel obs 定位为明确 limitation + future work，proprioceptive 设定为 controlled baseline。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # GROUP 1: Walker Walk Multi-Seed Replication\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: >\n      复现 CIVO collapse 的多 seed 验证。008d 配置 (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8)。\n      Registry 已完成: 009e (s1) + 009b (s2)。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 131.08\n      seed1_nve_peak: 4.12\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 55000\n      seed1_collapse: true\n      seed1_collapse_type: \"classic_CIVO_value_driven\"\n      seed2_eval_105K: 267.93\n      seed2_nve_peak: 2.05\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 25000\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_self_correction: true\n      seed2_nve_final: 0.38\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x: \"2/2\"\n      cross_seed_collapse_rate: \"1/2\"\n      independent_collapse_rate: \"1/2 (008d s0 与 009e s1 共享 seed=1, 视为同一观测)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, 2/2 trained dt_emb seeds 均超过 NVE 1.5× 被接受为 CIVO 诊断标记的\n      强 supporting evidence。审稿人理解 collapse 是 stochastic 的——关键发现不是\n      \"必然崩溃\" 而是 \"trained dt_emb 可靠触发病态过估值 (NVE>1.5×)\"。\n      Seed 1 的经典 CIVO (value-driven, entropy ↓, NVE 1.78→2.09→4.12 加速) vs\n      Seed 2 的自我修正 (NVE 2.05→1.62→0.38 衰减) 被视为丰富了 CIVO 动态的理解，\n      而非削弱了 claim。Sustained vs transient NVE>1.5× 的差异性（seed 1 连续3个\n      checkpoint 维持>1.5× → 不可逆; seed 2 仅一次突破 → 自我修正）与 Henderson\n      et al. 2018 的早期随机性影响结论一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Walker 008d Cross-Seed Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE_peak\", \"NVE_peak_step\", \"Collapse?\", \"Pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0 (008d)\", \"82.75\", \"4.12\", \"55K\", \"Yes\", \"Value-driven, entropy ↓\"]\n          - [\"s1 (009e)\", \"131.08\", \"4.12\", \"55K\", \"Yes\", \"Same seed as s0, deterministic replication\"]\n          - [\"s2 (009b)\", \"267.93\", \"2.05\", \"25K\", \"No\", \"Transient NVE → self-correction\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Learning curves (eval + NVE) for 008d s0/s1/s2 overlaid, showing divergence point at ~35K\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 核心证据：trained dt_emb 可靠触发 NVE>1.5× (2/2 independent seeds)。\n      Collapse 是 stochastic (1/2)，但 diagnostic marker 是 deterministic。\n      Best 档审稿人接受这一区分，不要求 deterministic collapse。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: >\n      C2 因果控制的多 seed 验证。008f 配置 (dt=2, subsample ON, dt_embed_dim=0, H=8)。\n      Registry: 009f (s1) killed → 使用替代 seeds (008f_s3, 008f_s4); 009c (s2) done。\n    expected_results:\n      seed2_eval_105K: 148.34\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.26\n      seed2_nve_105K: 1.14\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed3_eval_105K: 363.8\n      seed3_nve_peak: \"<1.5x\"\n      seed3_collapse: false\n      seed4_eval_105K: 306.5\n      seed4_nve_peak: 1.41\n      seed4_nve_105K: 0.58\n      seed4_collapse: false\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x: \"0/3\"\n      reward_MAE_baseline_ratio: \"~75x\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, 0/3 seeds 超过 NVE 1.5× 被接受为 dt_embedding 因果控制的决定性证据。\n      与 008d 的 2/2 形成 5/5 完美分离（trained 2/2 exceed, untrained 0/3 never exceed）。\n      审稿人注意到 009c 的 NVE=1.14@105K 接近但未达 1.5× threshold，且 008f_s4 的\n      transient NVE=1.41@85K 也在 threshold 以下——threshold 的区分力成立。\n      008f reward_MAE=0.747（baseline 75×）是已知 trade-off: 去掉 dt_embedding 后 reward\n      head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2。审稿人接受这不削弱因果结论——因果控制实验证明的是\n      \"去掉 X → 无崩溃\"，不需要 reward 预测同样好。R8 被 preempt。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 008f Causal Control Cross-Seed\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE_peak\", \"NVE@105K\", \"CIVO?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0 (008f)\", \"503\", \"1.02\", \"0.30\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"s2 (009c)\", \"148.34\", \"1.26\", \"1.14\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"s3\", \"363.8\", \"<1.5\", \"—\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"s4\", \"306.5\", \"1.41\", \"0.58\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE trajectories: 008d seeds (red, above 1.5× line) vs 008f seeds (blue, below 1.5× line)\"\n    analysis: >\n      与 008d 2/2 对比，形成 trained vs untrained dt_emb 的完美二分类。\n      Best 档审稿人视 008f 为 \"definitive causal control\"，008f 的低 eval 被理解为\n      因果控制实验的预期代价。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: >\n      C3 value growth suppression 多 seed 验证。008a 配置 (dt=2, subsample OFF, trained\n      dt_emb unexposed to dt>1 data, H=15)。Registry 已完成: 008a_unexposed_s1, s2。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 630.91\n      seed1_ve_ratio_105K: 0.43\n      seed1_civo_alert: 0\n      seed1_delta_ve: -0.0028\n      seed2_eval_105K: 899.4\n      seed2_ve_ratio_105K: 0.333\n      seed2_civo_alert: 0\n      seed2_delta_ve: -0.003\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x: \"0/2\"\n      cross_seed_eval_mean: 765.2\n      cross_seed_eval_range: \"631-899\"\n      vs_baseline_mean: \"83.5%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, unexposed dt_emb（trained 但训练数据中无 dt>1 transition）的两个新 seed\n      均展现 value suppression + 无 CIVO。Seed 2 特别强 (899.4 = 98% baseline)。\n      Cross-seed 均值 765 (83.5% baseline) 显著优于 008f (均值 ~330, 36% baseline)。\n      审稿人将此解读为: 真正有害的不是 dt_embedding 本身的存在，而是当 training data\n      中含有 dt>1 transitions 时 dt_embedding 学到 dt-specific representations。\n      这强化了 C2 的机制性解释（RSSM fidelity gap + learned conditioning amplification），\n      而非简单的 \"有 dt_emb = 坏\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 008a Unexposed Cross-Seed\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"VE ratio@105K\", \"NVE@105K\", \"Pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0 (008a)\", \"777.66\", \"0.386\", \"0.59\", \"Zigzag recovery, 2 V-cycles\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"630.91\", \"0.43\", \"~0.65\", \"Rising trend\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"899.4\", \"0.333\", \"~0.51\", \"Strong convergence, near-baseline\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Learning curves: 008a 3 seeds vs baseline band, showing zigzag recovery pattern\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3 核心证据加强。3 seeds 一致展现 value suppression (NVE 0.51-0.65x)。\n      高 seed variance (631-899) 被理解为 dt>1 数据缺失导致的学习不稳定，\n      而非方法论缺陷。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (dt=1 imagination) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: >\n      C6 dt=1 imagination 效果验证。008e_v3 配置 (trained dt_emb, dt=1 imagination, subsample\n      ON, H=15)。Registry 已完成: s1 (success), s2 (collapsed non-CIVO)。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 869.88\n      seed1_nve_peak: 0.80\n      seed1_ve_ratio_105K: 0.527\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed1_gate_dt_1_frac: 1.0\n      seed2_eval_105K: 136.96\n      seed2_nve_peak: 3.78\n      seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n      seed2_collapse: true\n      seed2_collapse_onset: \"95K\"\n      seed2_actor_entropy_trend: \"rising (-5.21@85K → -3.83@105K)\"\n      seed2_gate_dt_1_frac: 1.0\n      cross_seed_collapse_rate: \"1/2\"\n      collapse_mechanism_difference: \"seed2 = eval-driven (Pathway B), not value-driven (Pathway A)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, C6 PARTIALLY FALSIFIED 被透明报告并获审稿人认可。dt=1 imagination\n      不能阻止崩溃 (1/2 seeds)，但崩溃机制与经典 CIVO 定性不同：\n      - 008d s0 (Pathway A): value 爆炸 → actor exploit → eval 下跌，entropy ↓\n      - 008e_v3 s2 (Pathway B): eval 先跌 → NVE 被动升高，entropy ↑ (策略变随机)\n      审稿人接受 \"trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability through multiple pathways\"\n      这一更深层洞察。009a baseline s2 在同期完全稳定 (618→596→836)，排除 seed\n      脆弱假说。这实际上丰富了论文贡献——CIVO 不是唯一的脆弱通道。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Pathway A vs Pathway B Collapse Dynamics\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"008d s0 (Pathway A)\", \"008e_v3 s2 (Pathway B)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Value change\", \"Explosive (60→138, +130%@55K)\", \"Moderate (339→384→340, +13%→-12%)\"]\n          - [\"Eval change\", \"Post-value (146→83, -43%)\", \"Leads (715→452→137, -81%)\"]\n          - [\"NVE driver\", \"Value numerator (value explosion)\", \"Eval denominator (eval crash)\"]\n          - [\"Actor entropy\", \"↓ (-3.47→-4.88, policy locks)\", \"↑ (-5.21→-3.83, policy destabilizes)\"]\n          - [\"Mechanism\", \"Critic overestimate → actor exploit\", \"Eval crash → value lag\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-axis plot: value + entropy trajectories for Pathway A and B, color-coded\"\n    analysis: >\n      C6 从 \"practical mitigation\" 降级为 \"mechanistic insight: trained dt_emb 创建\n      多条脆弱通道\"。Best 档审稿人视此为 honest reporting + deeper understanding，\n      而非 weakness。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag + H=8\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: >\n      诊断 dt_emb TRAINING 是否为 CIVO 必要条件。dt_embedding 保持随机初始化但 freeze\n      (requires_grad=False)。Registry 已完成: exp_015b。\n    expected_results:\n      eval_105K: 204.2\n      nve_85K: 0.467\n      nve_95K: 0.394\n      nve_105K: 0.42\n      collapse: false\n      actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n      actor_entropy_105K: -4.855\n      value_mean_105K: 56.212\n      gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n      collapse_mechanism: \"gradient_starvation_from_frozen_dt_emb\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, frozen dt_emb 不崩溃但性能很差 (204 = 22% baseline)。NVE 全程 0.39-0.47\n      (远低于 1.0×, critic 严重低估)，actor_loss → 0（梯度饥饿）。这确认了 dt_emb\n      的 TRAINING 是 CIVO 的必要条件——没有训练的 dt_embedding 只是噪声输入，\n      不会创建 RSSM 对精确 dt 信号的 co-adaptation。但 frozen embedding 引入了\n      新问题（梯度饥饿），证明这不是一个可行的 mitigation 方向。\n      审稿人将此视为 2×2 消融矩阵 (008a/008d/008f/015b) 的完成：\n      - 008d (trained + subsample ON): CIVO ✓\n      - 008a (trained + subsample OFF): No CIVO ✓ (unexposed)\n      - 008f (removed, subsample ON): No CIVO ✓ (no embedding)\n      - 015b (frozen + subsample ON): No CIVO ✓ (frozen)\n      只有 008d (trained AND exposed to dt>1 data) 产生 CIVO → training 是必要条件。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: dt_emb 2×2 Ablation Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"dt_emb state\", \"Exposed to dt>1?\", \"CIVO?\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE range\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"008d\", \"Trained\", \"Yes (subsample ON)\", \"Yes (2/2)\", \"82-131\", \"1.71-4.12\"]\n          - [\"008a\", \"Trained\", \"No (subsample OFF)\", \"No (0/3)\", \"631-899\", \"0.51-0.65\"]\n          - [\"008f\", \"Removed (dim=0)\", \"Yes\", \"No (0/4)\", \"148-503\", \"0.30-1.41\"]\n          - [\"015b\", \"Frozen (random init)\", \"Yes\", \"No (0/1)\", \"204\", \"0.39-0.47\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 grid: eval trajectories for each ablation cell\"\n    analysis: >\n      闭合因果推理: dt_emb training + exposure to dt>1 data 两个条件同时满足时才触发 CIVO。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: >\n      缩小 008e_v3 (dt=1 imagination) 崩溃概率估计区间。Registry 已完成: s3 + s4。\n    expected_results:\n      seed3_eval_105K: 92.7\n      seed3_nve_peak: 4.02\n      seed3_collapse: true\n      seed3_collapse_onset: \"85K-95K\"\n      seed3_actor_entropy_final: -4.892\n      seed4_eval_105K: 899.3\n      seed4_nve_peak: 0.99\n      seed4_collapse: false\n      total_008e_v3_collapse_rate: \"2/4 (50%)\"\n      collapse_pathway_breakdown: \"s2 = Pathway B (eval-driven, entropy ↑); s3 = mixed (entropy remains low)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, 2/4 崩溃率 (50%) 与 008d 的 1/2 (50%) 完全一致——dt=1 imagination\n      未降低崩溃概率。这是 C6 PARTIALLY FALSIFIED 的最有力量化证据。\n      s3 崩溃 (NVE 4.02, entropy stays low at -4.892) 引入了第三种可能的动态模式，\n      但 best 档审稿人不要求对每个 seed 的机制差异做完整解释——4 seeds 确认 50%\n      崩溃率已经足够。核心结论: trained dt_embedding 是根本脆弱源，dt=1 imagination\n      只消除了一条特定通道 (Pathway A) 但不消除全部通道。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 008e_v3 Cross-Seed Summary (dt=1 imagination)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE_peak\", \"Collapse?\", \"Pathway\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s1 (008e_v3)\", \"869.9\", \"0.80\", \"No\", \"Healthy\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"137.0\", \"3.78\", \"Yes\", \"B (eval-driven, entropy ↑)\"]\n          - [\"s3\", \"92.7\", \"4.02\", \"Yes\", \"Mixed (entropy stays low)\"]\n          - [\"s4\", \"899.3\", \"0.99\", \"No\", \"Healthy\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-seed eval trajectories with collapse markers, showing 50% divergence\"\n    analysis: >\n      50% collapse rate 确认 dt=1 imagination 非有效 mitigation。Best 档审稿人\n      视此为诚实报告 + 对 trained dt_emb 多通道脆弱性的系统性证据。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # GROUP 2: Cheetah Run Cross-Environment Validation\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: >\n      第二 DMC 环境基准线。Registry 已有 5 seeds (023a/023b/023_s2/s3/s4)。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_final: 624.7\n      seed1_eval_final: 520.3\n      seed2_eval_final: 645.4\n      seed3_eval_final: 642.13\n      seed4_eval_final: 537.03\n      cross_seed_mean: 593.9\n      cross_seed_std: 56.8\n      cross_seed_range: \"520-645\"\n      ve_ratio_converged: \"0.65-0.70\"\n      ve_ratio_stable_from: \"150K+\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Cheetah baseline 提供了 NVE 归一化的可靠分母。5 seeds 的一致性\n      (std=56.8, CV=9.6%) 表明 Cheetah 环境有适度但可接受的 seed variance。\n      VE ratio 收敛到 0.65-0.70 (类似 Walker 的 0.69-0.72)，支持 NVE 归一化方法\n      在跨环境的适用性。审稿人接受 5 seeds 足够建立可靠 baseline。\n      s4 的 194K→204K eval 骤降 (537→302) 被确认为 transient fluctuation\n      (延长到 300K 恢复到 642)，不是 instability。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cheetah Baseline Cross-Seed\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval final\", \"Peak eval\", \"VE ratio converged\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"624.7\", \"624.7\", \"~0.67\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"520.3\", \"572.9\", \"~0.65\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"645.4\", \"645.4\", \"~0.68\"]\n          - [\"s3\", \"642.1\", \"685.9\", \"~0.69\"]\n          - [\"s4\", \"537.0 (ext→642)\", \"642.3\", \"~0.66\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah baseline 5-seed learning curves with IQM band\"\n    analysis: >\n      Robust baseline。Cross-seed IQM ~600，用于所有 Cheetah CIVO 实验的归一化。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: >\n      Cheetah 环境 CIVO 复现。Registry: 010b (s1 eval 51.7, NVE 8.27) + 010b_s0\n      (eval 0.83, NVE 70.64)。需 seed 2 预测。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_final: 0.83\n      seed0_nve_peak: 70.64\n      seed0_collapse: true\n      seed1_eval_final: 51.7\n      seed1_nve_peak: 8.27\n      seed1_collapse: true\n      seed2_eval_final_predicted: 38.5\n      seed2_nve_peak_predicted: 12.4\n      seed2_nve_peak_step_predicted: \"55K\"\n      seed2_collapse_predicted: true\n      cross_seed_collapse_rate: \"3/3\"\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x: \"3/3\"\n      cheetah_vs_walker_severity: \"Cheetah NVE peaks 2-9× higher than Walker (8-70× vs 2-4×)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Cheetah CIVO 比 Walker 更严重但 100% 一致。Cheetah 的 3/3 崩溃率\n      (vs Walker 的 ~50%) 表明环境复杂度放大了 CIVO——更复杂的 dynamics → 更大的\n      RSSM fidelity gap → 更强的 value overestimation feedback loop。\n      NVE peaks 远高于 Walker (8-70× vs 2-4×) 同样支持这一解读。\n      审稿人将跨环境 NVE severity 差异视为支持 \"CIVO severity scales with RSSM prediction\n      difficulty\" 的证据——这不是 noise，而是 signal。\n      Seed 2 预测基于 s0/s1 的模式: Cheetah 中 CIVO 更可靠 (100% vs Walker 50%)，\n      NVE peak 在 8-70× 范围内。保守预测 12.4× 处于该范围中段。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cheetah CIVO Trigger Cross-Seed\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval final\", \"NVE_peak\", \"Collapse?\", \"Baseline%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"0.83\", \"70.64\", \"Yes\", \"0.1%\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"51.7\", \"8.27\", \"Yes\", \"8.7%\"]\n          - [\"s2 (predicted)\", \"38.5\", \"12.4\", \"Yes\", \"6.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah CIVO: NVE trajectories showing extreme overestimation peaks\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 100% collapse rate 加强了 C1 + C2。与 Walker 的 severity 差异\n      提供了额外的 mechanistic insight。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: >\n      Cheetah 因果控制。Registry: 024b_s0 (eval 96.5, no CIVO), 024b_s1 (eval 77.3).\n      Need seed 2 prediction.\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_final: 96.5\n      seed0_nve_peak: 0.2\n      seed0_civo: false\n      seed1_eval_final: 77.3\n      seed1_nve_peak: 0.1\n      seed1_civo: false\n      seed2_eval_final_predicted: 88.2\n      seed2_nve_peak_predicted: 0.15\n      seed2_civo_predicted: false\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x: \"0/3\"\n      cross_seed_eval_mean: 87.3\n      vs_baseline: \"14.7%\"\n      reward_prediction_quality: \"severely degraded (similar to Walker 008f pattern)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Cheetah no-dt-emb 完美复现 Walker 008f 的模式: 0/3 CIVO, 但 eval\n      严重下降 (14.7% baseline)。NVE 全程极低 (<0.2×)，连 baseline 水平的 value\n      估计都无法达到。这不是好的 mitigation (性能损失太大)，但作为因果控制完美:\n      去掉 dt_embedding → CIVO 消失。\n      Cheetah 的 dt-emb-removal 性能损失 (14.7%) 比 Walker (36%) 更大，这合理——\n      Cheetah 的更复杂 dynamics 意味着缺失 temporal information 的代价更高。\n      审稿人接受 008f/024b 是因果控制而非推荐方案。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cheetah Causal Control (no dt_emb)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval final\", \"NVE_peak\", \"CIVO?\", \"Baseline%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"96.5\", \"0.2\", \"No\", \"15.4%\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"77.3\", \"0.1\", \"No\", \"12.3%\"]\n          - [\"s2 (predicted)\", \"88.2\", \"0.15\", \"No\", \"14.8%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah: CIVO trigger (red) vs no-dt-emb control (blue) eval curves\"\n    analysis: >\n      跨环境因果控制复现。dt_embedding removal 的 5/5 (Walker) + 3/3 (Cheetah) = 8/8\n      CIVO prevention rate。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: >\n      Cheetah unexposed dt_emb 验证 (C3)。Registry: 008a_cheetah_s0 (532.35, NVE 0.49),\n      s1 (504.38, NVE 0.478). Need seed 2 prediction.\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 532.35\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.49\n      seed0_civo: false\n      seed1_eval_105K: 504.38\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.478\n      seed1_civo: false\n      seed2_eval_105K_predicted: 518.6\n      seed2_nve_105K_predicted: 0.48\n      seed2_civo_predicted: false\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x: \"0/3\"\n      cross_seed_eval_mean: 518.4\n      vs_baseline: \"87.3%\"\n      vs_no_dt_emb: \"5.9x better (518 vs 87)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Cheetah unexposed dt_emb 展现出与 Walker 008a 一致的 pattern:\n      接近 baseline 的性能 (87% vs Walker 83.5%), NVE 全程受抑 (0.48-0.49×),\n      无 CIVO。这与 no-dt-emb (plan_022, 14.7% baseline) 形成鲜明对比——\n      保留 dt_embedding 但不暴露于 dt>1 data 是明显更优的方案。\n      跨环境一致性极高 (Walker 83.5% vs Cheetah 87.3% of baseline)，审稿人将此\n      视为 C3 在第二环境的强复现。Seed variance 在 Cheetah 很小 (504-532, 2.7%)\n      vs Walker 的较大 variance (631-899, 17.4%)——可能因为 Cheetah 的 simpler\n      reward structure 导致更一致的学习。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cheetah Unexposed dt_emb (C3 validation)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE@105K\", \"CIVO?\", \"Baseline%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"532.4\", \"0.49\", \"No\", \"89.7%\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"504.4\", \"0.48\", \"No\", \"84.9%\"]\n          - [\"s2 (predicted)\", \"518.6\", \"0.48\", \"No\", \"87.3%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment C3 comparison: Walker 008a vs Cheetah unexposed, normalized\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3 跨环境验证完成。Unexposed dt_emb 在两环境均提供 >83% baseline 性能和 NVE<0.5×。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # GROUP 3: Cartpole Swingup (Non-Locomotion Validation)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: >\n      非运动型 DMC 环境基准线。DreamerV3 proprioceptive Cartpole Swingup。\n      全部为预测数据。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_final_predicted: 842.3\n      seed1_eval_final_predicted: 818.6\n      seed2_eval_final_predicted: 854.1\n      cross_seed_mean_predicted: 838.3\n      cross_seed_std_predicted: 18.0\n      convergence_step_predicted: \"~80K (faster than Walker ~100K due to simpler dynamics)\"\n      ve_ratio_converged_predicted: \"0.68-0.73\"\n      eval_peak_range_predicted: \"850-870\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Cartpole Swingup baseline 提供非运动环境的参考点。DreamerV3 在\n      proprioceptive Cartpole 上通常达到 ~830-860 (基于公开 benchmark)。\n      收敛更快 (~80K vs Walker ~100K) 因为 observation space 更小 (5D vs 24D)\n      且 dynamics 更简单。VE ratio 收敛到类似 Walker/Cheetah 的 ~0.70 范围，\n      表明 DreamerV3 的 value calibration 跨环境一致。\n      低 seed variance (CV ~2.1%) 预期因为 Cartpole 的 simpler dynamics 导致\n      更一致的学习。审稿人接受这作为第三环境 baseline。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cartpole Swingup Baseline (predicted)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval final\", \"VE ratio\", \"Convergence step\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"842.3\", \"0.71\", \"~78K\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"818.6\", \"0.69\", \"~82K\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"854.1\", \"0.73\", \"~76K\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole baseline learning curves with Walker/Cheetah normalized comparison\"\n    analysis: >\n      非运动环境 baseline 确立。对 C1/C2/C3 的跨 task-type 验证至关重要。\n      但 best 档 narrative 指出 Walker+Cheetah+PickCube 已足够——Cartpole\n      是 additional strength, not a requirement。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: >\n      非运动环境 CIVO 复现。全部为预测数据。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K_predicted: 127.4\n      seed0_nve_peak_predicted: 3.21\n      seed0_nve_peak_step_predicted: \"55K\"\n      seed0_collapse_predicted: true\n      seed1_eval_105K_predicted: 612.7\n      seed1_nve_peak_predicted: 1.83\n      seed1_nve_peak_step_predicted: \"45K\"\n      seed1_collapse_predicted: false\n      seed1_self_correction_predicted: true\n      seed2_eval_105K_predicted: 95.6\n      seed2_nve_peak_predicted: 4.47\n      seed2_nve_peak_step_predicted: \"65K\"\n      seed2_collapse_predicted: true\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x_predicted: \"3/3\"\n      cross_seed_collapse_rate_predicted: \"2/3\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Cartpole CIVO 表现与 Walker 类似而非 Cheetah。Cartpole 的简单\n      dynamics 意味着 RSSM fidelity gap 中等 (类似 Walker)，所以 CIVO severity\n      处于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间。3/3 seeds 超过 NVE 1.5× (诊断标记一致),\n      2/3 collapse (类似 Walker 50% rate)。\n      Seed 1 自我修正模式与 009b (Walker) 一致——transient NVE>1.5× 后衰减。\n      这跨环境复现了 \"sustained vs transient NVE\" 的 stochastic divergence 模式。\n      审稿人将此视为 CIVO 机制跨 task type 的强验证——不仅限于 locomotion。\n      NVE peaks (1.83-4.47) 处于 Walker (2.05-4.12) 类似范围，而非 Cheetah 的\n      极端范围 (8-70×)，支持 \"CIVO severity ~ RSSM difficulty\" 假设。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cartpole CIVO Trigger (predicted)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE_peak\", \"Collapse?\", \"Pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"127.4\", \"3.21\", \"Yes\", \"Classic CIVO\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"612.7\", \"1.83\", \"No\", \"Transient → self-correction\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"95.6\", \"4.47\", \"Yes\", \"Classic CIVO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment NVE peak comparison: Walker / Cheetah / Cartpole\"\n    analysis: >\n      非运动环境 CIVO 确认。3/3 NVE>1.5× + 2/3 collapse, 与 locomotion 一致。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: >\n      非运动环境因果控制。全部为预测数据。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K_predicted: 312.4\n      seed0_nve_peak_predicted: 0.35\n      seed0_civo_predicted: false\n      seed1_eval_105K_predicted: 278.9\n      seed1_nve_peak_predicted: 0.42\n      seed1_civo_predicted: false\n      seed2_eval_105K_predicted: 335.1\n      seed2_nve_peak_predicted: 0.28\n      seed2_civo_predicted: false\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x_predicted: \"0/3\"\n      cross_seed_eval_mean_predicted: 308.8\n      vs_baseline_predicted: \"36.8%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Cartpole no-dt-emb 复现 Walker/Cheetah 的因果控制模式:\n      0/3 CIVO, eval 显著低于 baseline (36.8%)。\n      Cartpole 的 eval loss (63.2%) 介于 Walker (64%) 和 Cheetah (85.3%) 之间，\n      与环境复杂度的排序一致 (Cheetah > Cartpole > Walker in temporal info value)。\n      但这可能存在混淆 (Cartpole 的 temporal info 可能天然不如 locomotion 重要)，\n      best 档审稿人不深究此点——关键是 CIVO prevention = 100%。\n      跨三环境汇总: dt_emb removal → 0/11 CIVO (Walker 0/4 + Cheetah 0/3 + Cartpole 0/3 + PickCube 0/1)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cartpole Causal Control (predicted)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE_peak\", \"CIVO?\", \"Baseline%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"312.4\", \"0.35\", \"No\", \"37.1%\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"278.9\", \"0.42\", \"No\", \"33.1%\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"335.1\", \"0.28\", \"No\", \"39.9%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment causal control summary bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      第三环境因果控制完成。dt_emb removal → 0/11 CIVO prevention 跨所有环境。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # GROUP 4: Analysis Tasks (0-1 GPU hours)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: >\n      RSSM fidelity gap 量化。Registry 已完成: exp_rssm_fidelity_analysis。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_dt1_obs_MSE: 13.49\n      baseline_dt2_obs_MSE: 27.50\n      baseline_obs_gap: 2.04\n      baseline_dt1_reward_MAE: 0.0102\n      baseline_dt2_reward_MAE: 0.0159\n      baseline_reward_gap: 1.56\n      008d_dt1_obs_MSE: 41.31\n      008d_dt2_obs_MSE: 53.67\n      008d_obs_gap: 1.30\n      008d_dt1_reward_MAE: 0.0568\n      008d_dt2_reward_MAE: 0.1579\n      008d_reward_gap: 2.78\n      008f_dt1_obs_MSE: 8.01\n      008f_dt2_obs_MSE: 22.04\n      008f_obs_gap: 2.75\n      008f_dt1_reward_MAE: 0.7469\n      008f_dt2_reward_MAE: 0.7526\n      008f_reward_gap: 1.01\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, RSSM fidelity 表是 C2 机制解释的核心定量支撑。关键 insight:\n      (1) 008d obs_gap 仅 1.30× (看似小), 但 dt1 绝对误差 41.31 已是 baseline 的 3×\n      → 模型本身已崩塌，低 gap ratio 是误导性的。论文必须并排呈现绝对值和比率。\n      (2) 008d reward_gap 2.78× → trained dt_emb 让 reward head 学到了精确的\n      dt-specific reward predictions, 但这个精确度建立在 RSSM 的 imprecise states 上\n      → 系统性 reward 过估。\n      (3) 008f reward_gap 1.01× → no dt_emb 时 reward head 完全无法区分 dt=1/dt=2,\n      reward_MAE=0.747 (baseline 75×), 这是 \"去掉 dt_emb 代价太大\" 的定量证据。\n      审稿人视此表为 \"smoking gun\"——不是模型不好，而是 conditioning 让模型在错误的\n      基础上过于 confident。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1 (论文): RSSM Fidelity Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"dt1 obs_MSE\", \"dt2 obs_MSE\", \"obs gap\", \"dt1 rew_MAE\", \"dt2 rew_MAE\", \"rew gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline (dt=1)\", \"13.49\", \"27.50\", \"2.04×\", \"0.010\", \"0.016\", \"1.56×\"]\n          - [\"008d (trained dt_emb)\", \"41.31\", \"53.67\", \"1.30×*\", \"0.057\", \"0.158\", \"2.78×\"]\n          - [\"008f (no dt_emb)\", \"8.01\", \"22.04\", \"2.75×\", \"0.747\", \"0.753\", \"1.01×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: absolute errors (grouped by model) + ratio annotations\"\n      - \"* 008d low obs gap ratio is misleading — absolute errors are 3× baseline\"\n    analysis: >\n      Figure 4 / Table 1 核心证据。三模型对比完整揭示 trained dt_emb 如何创建\n      CIVO 的 forward-pass 基础。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: >\n      从现有 metrics.jsonl 提取 actor_entropy trajectories。0 GPU cost。\n    expected_results:\n      008d_s0_entropy_35K: -3.465\n      008d_s0_entropy_45K: -4.575\n      008d_s0_entropy_55K: -4.879\n      008d_s0_trend: \"monotonic decrease → policy locks onto overestimated actions\"\n      008e_v3_s2_entropy_85K: -5.208\n      008e_v3_s2_entropy_95K: -4.529\n      008e_v3_s2_entropy_105K: -3.828\n      008e_v3_s2_trend: \"increase during collapse → policy destabilizes\"\n      008a_s0_entropy_105K_predicted: -5.1\n      008a_s0_trend: \"stable convergence to low entropy (normal learning)\"\n      baseline_entropy_converged_predicted: \"-5.2 to -5.5\"\n      016e_entropy_comparison: \"SGS preserves ~1.0-1.3 nats higher entropy through 35-55K\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, actor entropy 分析提供了 Pathway A vs B 的独立定量区分。\n      Pathway A (008d s0): entropy 单调下降 (-3.47 → -4.88) = actor 变得越来越\n      deterministic，exploit overestimated value regions。这是经典 CIVO 签名。\n      Pathway B (008e_v3 s2): entropy 上升 (-5.21 → -3.83) = policy 在崩溃期间\n      变随机，失去已学结构。这与 value-driven exploitation 相反。\n      健康配置 (008a, baseline): entropy 稳定收敛到 ~-5.2 (正常确定性策略)。\n      SGS (016e) 的高 entropy (+1.0-1.3 nats) 解释了它为何延迟但不阻止 CIVO:\n      更多探索暂时抵消了 value overestimation, 但无法永久阻止。\n      审稿人视此为 Figure 级别的 supporting evidence, 加强了论文的机制性叙事。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Actor Entropy Signatures\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"Entropy@35K\", \"Entropy@55K\", \"Entropy@105K\", \"Trend\", \"Classification\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline s0\", \"-4.2\", \"-5.0\", \"-5.3\", \"Converging ↓\", \"Healthy\"]\n          - [\"008a s0 (unexposed)\", \"-3.8\", \"-4.6\", \"-5.1\", \"Converging ↓\", \"Healthy\"]\n          - [\"008d s0 (CIVO)\", \"-3.47\", \"-4.88\", \"—(collapsed)\", \"Accelerating ↓\", \"Pathway A\"]\n          - [\"008e_v3 s2\", \"-5.12\", \"-5.12\", \"-3.83\", \"Rising ↑ at collapse\", \"Pathway B\"]\n          - [\"016e (SGS)\", \"-2.12\", \"-3.62\", \"—(collapsed)\", \"Delayed ↓\", \"SGS-modified CIVO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure: Entropy trajectories — healthy (blue) vs Pathway A (red) vs Pathway B (orange)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Entropy 分析提供了 collapse 动态的独立验证维度。Best 档审稿人将此\n      视为 mechanism-level claim 的有力 supplementary evidence。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: >\n      V(s) vs Monte Carlo return 分布对比。1 GPU hour for trajectory collection。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_v_mc_correlation_predicted: 0.92\n      baseline_v_mc_bias_predicted: \"+2-5% (slight optimism, normal)\"\n      008d_v_mc_correlation_35K_predicted: 0.71\n      008d_v_mc_correlation_55K_predicted: 0.38\n      008d_v_mc_bias_55K_predicted: \"+180% (extreme optimism at dt>1 states)\"\n      008d_dt2_specific_bias_predicted: \"+250% at dt=2 imagined states vs +40% at dt=1\"\n      008a_v_mc_correlation_predicted: 0.85\n      008a_v_mc_bias_predicted: \"-5% (slight pessimism, consistent with NVE<1.0×)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, distributional analysis 升级了 v/e ratio proxy 的说服力。\n      关键发现: 008d 的 value overestimation 不是 uniform 的——它集中在 dt>1\n      imagined states (+250%), 而 dt=1 states 仅有 +40% 偏差。这直接证明了\n      trained dt_embedding + RSSM fidelity gap 的交互效应。\n      008a 的轻微 pessimism (-5%) 与 NVE<1.0× 一致，说明 unexposed dt_emb\n      实际上倾向于 underestimate value (safe bias)。\n      审稿人视此为 \"beyond a crude proxy\" (preempt R3) 的关键补充分析。\n      如果时间不足, best 档 narrative 中 v/e ratio proxy 仍被接受 (R3 被 preempt\n      by the 4/4 NVE threshold + AUROC analysis)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: V(s) vs MC Return Statistics\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"V-MC correlation\", \"Mean bias\", \"dt>1 specific bias\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline\", \"0.92\", \"+3%\", \"N/A (dt=1 only)\"]\n          - [\"008d@35K\", \"0.71\", \"+85%\", \"+160% at dt=2\"]\n          - [\"008d@55K\", \"0.38\", \"+180%\", \"+250% at dt=2\"]\n          - [\"008a@105K\", \"0.85\", \"-5%\", \"N/A (unexposed)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plots: V(s) vs MC return, color-coded by dt, with regression lines\"\n    analysis: >\n      P2 优先级, 但若完成则显著加强 C2 的 mechanistic depth。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: >\n      跟踪 dt=1 和 dt=2 embedding vectors 在训练过程中的分离。0 GPU cost。\n    expected_results:\n      initial_cosine_sim_predicted: 0.02\n      cosine_sim_15K_predicted: -0.12\n      cosine_sim_35K_predicted: -0.38\n      cosine_sim_55K_predicted: -0.52\n      cosine_sim_105K_predicted: -0.61\n      embedding_norm_ratio_dt2_vs_dt1_predicted: 1.34\n      divergence_onset_predicted: \"10-15K (coincides with reward head learning dt-specific predictions)\"\n      frozen_cosine_sim_predicted: 0.02  # constant (frozen embedding)\n      008f_predicted: \"N/A (dt_embed_dim=0)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, embedding cosine similarity 提供了 trained dt_emb 如何 diverge 的\n      可视化证据。dt=1 和 dt=2 embeddings 从近似随机 (cos~0) 分化到显著负相关\n      (cos~-0.5 to -0.6)。分化 onset (~15K) 与 reward head 开始区分 dt=1/dt=2\n      的时间一致 (RSSM fidelity 表中 008d reward_gap 从 15K 开始明显 > 1.0)。\n      Embedding norm ratio >1 表明 dt=2 embedding 的幅度更大——可能因为 RSSM\n      需要更强的 conditioning signal 来处理较大的 temporal gap。\n      审稿人视此为 minor supplementary analysis。不会改变论文的核心评估，\n      但为 appendix/supplementary 提供了有用的可视化。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: dt_embedding Cosine Similarity Evolution\"\n        columns: [\"Step\", \"cos(emb_dt1, emb_dt2)\", \"||emb_dt2|| / ||emb_dt1||\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 (init)\", \"0.02\", \"1.00\"]\n          - [\"15K\", \"-0.12\", \"1.08\"]\n          - [\"35K\", \"-0.38\", \"1.21\"]\n          - [\"55K\", \"-0.52\", \"1.30\"]\n          - [\"105K\", \"-0.61\", \"1.34\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: cosine similarity over training steps, annotated with CIVO onset\"\n    analysis: >\n      P2 supplementary analysis。Embedding divergence 与 CIVO onset 的时间相关性\n      提供了额外的 mechanistic link。\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: >\n      从所有已完成实验计算 NVE 分类性能。0 GPU cost。AUROC + Youden-optimal threshold。\n    expected_results:\n      total_data_points: 29\n      environments: 4\n      AUROC: 0.969\n      threshold_sweep:\n        t1.0: {sensitivity: 1.00, specificity: 0.72, accuracy: 0.83, youden_J: 0.72}\n        t1.2: {sensitivity: 0.96, specificity: 0.86, accuracy: 0.90, youden_J: 0.82}\n        t1.3: {sensitivity: 0.93, specificity: 0.93, accuracy: 0.93, youden_J: 0.86}\n        t1.5: {sensitivity: 0.93, specificity: 0.97, accuracy: 0.95, youden_J: 0.90}\n        t1.7: {sensitivity: 0.86, specificity: 1.00, accuracy: 0.93, youden_J: 0.86}\n        t2.0: {sensitivity: 0.75, specificity: 1.00, accuracy: 0.88, youden_J: 0.75}\n      youden_optimal_threshold: 1.53\n      youden_optimal_J: 0.905\n      classification_at_1.5x:\n        true_positives: 13  # trained dt_emb seeds exceeding 1.5×\n        true_negatives: 14  # non-CIVO seeds never exceeding 1.5×\n        false_positives: 1  # non-CIVO seed transiently approaching 1.5× (borderline)\n        false_negatives: 1  # trained dt_emb seed briefly touching 1.5× but self-correcting before sustained\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, AUROC=0.969 配合 Youden-optimal 独立收敛到 1.53× 化解了 in-sample\n      calibration 质疑 (R10)。审稿人认可:\n      (1) Youden-optimal 1.53× 与预设 1.5× 的独立收敛不是 overfitting——如果 threshold\n      是 post-hoc 选择, Youden optimal 不太可能恰好落在同一位置。\n      (2) 4 环境 × 多 config 提供了 reasonable diversity, 尽管仍是 in-sample。\n      (3) 1-2 个 borderline cases (false positive/negative) 的存在反而增加可信度——\n      perfect 分类在小样本下更像 overfitting。\n      审稿人建议 held-out validation 作为 future work, 但不作为 major weakness。\n      NVE 在不同 reward scale 下的 generalization boundary 被明确讨论 (Cheetah NVE\n      peaks 远高于 Walker, 但 threshold 仍有效分类)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: NVE Threshold Sensitivity (AUROC=0.969)\"\n        columns: [\"Threshold\", \"Sensitivity\", \"Specificity\", \"Accuracy\", \"Youden J\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1.0×\", \"1.00\", \"0.72\", \"0.83\", \"0.72\"]\n          - [\"1.2×\", \"0.96\", \"0.86\", \"0.90\", \"0.82\"]\n          - [\"1.3×\", \"0.93\", \"0.93\", \"0.93\", \"0.86\"]\n          - [\"**1.5×**\", \"**0.93**\", \"**0.97**\", \"**0.95**\", \"**0.90**\"]\n          - [\"1.7×\", \"0.86\", \"1.00\", \"0.93\", \"0.86\"]\n          - [\"2.0×\", \"0.75\", \"1.00\", \"0.88\", \"0.75\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Youden-Optimal Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"AUROC\", \"0.969\"]\n          - [\"Youden-optimal threshold\", \"1.53×\"]\n          - [\"Preselected threshold\", \"1.50×\"]\n          - [\"Convergence gap\", \"0.03× (2%)\"]\n          - [\"N data points\", \"29\"]\n          - [\"N environments\", \"4\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC curve with AUROC annotation and Youden-optimal point marked\"\n      - \"Threshold vs accuracy/sensitivity/specificity trade-off curves\"\n    analysis: >\n      NVE 诊断的定量基础。AUROC 0.969 + Youden 独立收敛是论文最强的方法论贡献之一。\n      Best 档审稿人接受 with caveat (in-sample), 不降级为 major weakness。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # GROUP 5: Hopper Hop + Exploratory\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: >\n      第三 locomotion 环境。P2 优先级。全部为预测数据。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline:\n        seed0_eval_final_predicted: 232.4\n        seed1_eval_final_predicted: 178.6\n        seed2_eval_final_predicted: 256.8\n        mean_predicted: 222.6\n        std_predicted: 40.1\n        ve_ratio_converged_predicted: \"0.55-0.65\"\n      civo_trigger:\n        seed0_eval_final_predicted: 45.3\n        seed0_nve_peak_predicted: 5.62\n        seed0_collapse_predicted: true\n        seed1_eval_final_predicted: 123.8\n        seed1_nve_peak_predicted: 2.31\n        seed1_collapse_predicted: false\n        seed2_eval_final_predicted: 31.7\n        seed2_nve_peak_predicted: 7.84\n        seed2_collapse_predicted: true\n        cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x_predicted: \"3/3\"\n        cross_seed_collapse_rate_predicted: \"2/3\"\n      no_dt_emb:\n        seed0_eval_final_predicted: 72.5\n        seed0_nve_peak_predicted: 0.31\n        seed1_eval_final_predicted: 58.3\n        seed1_nve_peak_predicted: 0.25\n        seed2_eval_final_predicted: 84.1\n        seed2_nve_peak_predicted: 0.38\n        cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x_predicted: \"0/3\"\n        vs_baseline_predicted: \"32.2%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Hopper Hop 是 P2 额外验证——论文叙事不依赖它, 但若完成则强化\n      generalization claim。Hopper 是较难的 locomotion task (DreamerV3 baseline\n      ~180-260), seed variance 较大 (CV ~18%) 因为 hopping 任务对 policy\n      细微差异更敏感。\n      CIVO trigger 预测遵循 Walker 模式: 3/3 NVE>1.5×, 2/3 collapse。\n      NVE severity (2-8×) 介于 Walker (2-4×) 和 Cheetah (8-70×) 之间,\n      反映 Hopper dynamics 的中等复杂度。\n      No-dt-emb 预测 0/3 CIVO, eval ~32% baseline (类似 Walker/Cartpole)。\n      若完成, 跨环境 CIVO prevention 总计: Walker 0/4 + Cheetah 0/3 + PickCube 0/1\n      + Cartpole 0/3 + Hopper 0/3 = 0/14。\n      但 best 档审稿人已接受 3 环境足够——Hopper 是 bonus。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Hopper Hop 3×3 Summary (predicted)\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"Eval mean\", \"NVE>1.5× rate\", \"Collapse rate\", \"Baseline%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline\", \"222.6\", \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"100%\"]\n          - [\"CIVO trigger\", \"66.9\", \"3/3\", \"2/3\", \"30.1%\"]\n          - [\"No dt_emb\", \"71.6\", \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"32.2%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment summary: 4-5 environments × 3 configs heat map\"\n    analysis: >\n      P2 但若完成则为论文最强 generalization evidence。\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: >\n      P1 探索性实验: RSSM 预测不确定性超过阈值时截断 imagination rollout。\n      Walker Walk, dt=2, 1 seed。全部为预测数据。\n    expected_results:\n      eval_105K_predicted: 485.3\n      nve_peak_predicted: 1.42\n      nve_105K_predicted: 0.73\n      collapse_predicted: false\n      civo_prevented_predicted: true\n      vs_baseline_predicted: \"53.0%\"\n      effective_horizon_mean_predicted: 9.2\n      effective_horizon_std_predicted: 3.4\n      truncation_trigger_rate_predicted: \"38% of rollout steps\"\n      value_calibration_predicted: \"moderate underestimation (NVE 0.6-0.8×)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, uncertainty-gated truncation 是 Intervention Hierarchy 的潜在第四层\n      (Model-based gating)。预测它部分有效: NVE 保持 <1.5× (CIVO technically prevented),\n      但 eval 仅 53% baseline (truncation 过于激进, 缩短了有效 imagination horizon)。\n      这类似于 TCN 的困境: 足以阻止 CIVO 的干预强度也损害了学习。\n      Truncation rate 38% 表明 RSSM 在相当多的 rollout steps 上不确定——这本身\n      就是 RSSM fidelity gap 的直接度量。\n      审稿人可能将此视为 \"interesting pilot but needs more investigation\"——P1\n      定位合理, 不会升级为论文核心贡献, 但为 future work 提供了具体方向。\n      如果添加到 Intervention Hierarchy:\n      L4 (Model-based): Uncertainty truncation 1/1 prevents CIVO but 53% eval retention.\n      与 L3 TCN (2/8, 45-91% retention) 互补: 不同机制, 类似 trade-off。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Uncertainty-Gated Truncation Pilot\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"Comparison\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Eval@105K\", \"485.3\", \"53% baseline (vs TCN σ=0.2 68%)\"]\n          - [\"NVE_peak\", \"1.42\", \"Below 1.5× threshold\"]\n          - [\"Mean effective horizon\", \"9.2/15\", \"Truncation reduces useful imagination\"]\n          - [\"Truncation trigger rate\", \"38%\", \"RSSM uncertain at 38% of steps\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Effective horizon over training + NVE trajectory, showing truncation → NVE suppression\"\n    analysis: >\n      Pilot 结果支持 \"CIVO prevention ↔ learning quality trade-off\" 的系统性发现。\n      可选添加到 Intervention Hierarchy 作为 L4, 但非论文核心。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Aggregate: Cross-Experiment Synthesis Tables\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Aggregate: Intervention Hierarchy Final Table\"\n    plan_id: \"aggregate_intervention_hierarchy\"\n    description: >\n      论文核心 Table: 所有干预方法的系统性评估汇总。整合 C7 + C8 全部数据。\n    expected_results:\n      total_seeds_tested: 42\n      total_methods: 8\n      total_levels: 3\n      total_environments: 3\n      overall_CIVO_prevention_rate: \"4/36 (11.1%) — excluding embedding removal control\"\n      embedding_removal_rate: \"8/8 (100%) — removes the feature entirely\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Intervention Hierarchy 被认可为系统性贡献。审稿人看到的是:\n      8 种方法, 3 个干预层级, 3 个环境, 42 seeds——这是该类问题的首次系统性评估。\n      关键 narrative: 论文不是 \"我们试了一个方法失败了\", 而是 \"我们系统性地探索了\n      整个干预空间, 发现 CIVO fundamentally hard to mitigate through post-hoc interventions\"。\n      Gradient level (L1) 失败因为 forward-pass damage 不可逆;\n      Output level (L2) 失败因为 EMA anchor 被污染;\n      Representation level (L3) 在最优条件下偶尔成功但不可靠。\n      唯一 100% 有效的方法是移除 feature 本身——这不是 intervention, 是 surrender。\n      这为 future work 提供了明确方向: 需要 architectural solutions (THICK/Hieros\n      式分层时间抽象), 而非 post-hoc patches。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table (论文核心): Intervention Hierarchy\"\n        columns: [\"Level\", \"Method\", \"Success rate\", \"Best eval retention\", \"Primary failure mechanism\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"L1 Gradient\", \"Full SGS\", \"0/3\", \"49%\", \"Forward-pass damage irreducible\"]\n          - [\"L1 Gradient\", \"Obs-decoder SGS\", \"1/6\", \"79% (but critic destroyed)\", \"Compensatory amplification\"]\n          - [\"L1 Gradient\", \"Reward SGS\", \"0/2\", \"36%\", \"No-op (gradient ≠ causality)\"]\n          - [\"L2 Output\", \"RAVE ceil=2.0\", \"0/1\", \"3%\", \"EMA anchor pollution\"]\n          - [\"L2 Output\", \"RAVE ceil=1.5\", \"0/1\", \"8%\", \"EMA anchor pollution\"]\n          - [\"L3 Representation\", \"TCN σ=0.2\", \"2/8*\", \"91%/45% (high variance)\", \"Dose insufficient in complex envs\"]\n          - [\"L3 Representation\", \"TCN σ=0.5\", \"0/3\", \"40%\", \"Overdose (Walker) / Underdose (Cheetah)\"]\n          - [\"L3 Representation\", \"TCN σ=1.0\", \"1/1†\", \"27%\", \"Learning destroyed by noise\"]\n          - [\"**Control**\", \"**dt_emb removal**\", \"**8/8**\", \"**15-37%**\", \"**(removes feature)**\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure: Intervention Hierarchy pyramid visualization with success rates\"\n      - \"* 2/8 includes Walker-only σ=0.2 success; cross-env 0/4\"\n      - \"† Cheetah σ=1.0: technically prevents CIVO (NVE<0.21) but eval 27% → noise destroys learning\"\n    analysis: >\n      论文最重要的 contribution table。Best 档审稿人将此视为 \"systematic negative\n      results that save the community significant wasted effort\"。\n\n  - name: \"Aggregate: NVE Cross-Environment Classification\"\n    plan_id: \"aggregate_nve_classification\"\n    description: >\n      NVE≥1.5× 诊断标记跨环境汇总。\n    expected_results:\n      walker_trained_above_1.5x: \"5/5 (008d s0-s4)\"\n      walker_untrained_above_1.5x: \"0/7 (008f s0-s4 + 008a s0-s2)\"\n      cheetah_trained_above_1.5x: \"3/3 (010b s0-s1 + predicted s2)\"\n      cheetah_untrained_above_1.5x: \"0/5 (024b s0-s1 + 008a_cheetah s0-s1 + predicted)\"\n      pickcube_trained_above_1.5x: \"1/1 (019b)\"\n      pickcube_untrained_above_1.5x: \"0/0 (no control run)\"\n      total_AUROC: 0.969\n      total_sensitivity: 0.93\n      total_specificity: 0.97\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, NVE 跨环境分类汇总是论文 C2 的 capstone evidence。\n      Trained dt_emb → NVE>1.5× 在 9/9+ 个 independent observations 中成立\n      (部分 seeds 共享 seed number, 需去重)。Untrained → 0/12+ 超过 1.5×。\n      AUROC 0.969 在 4 环境 29 data points 上成立, 尽管是 in-sample。\n      审稿人接受 NVE≥1.5× 作为 \"reliable early-warning diagnostic for CIVO risk\n      in temporal-abstraction world-model RL\", 建议 held-out validation 作为 future work。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: NVE Cross-Environment Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Environment\", \"Trained dt_emb NVE>1.5×\", \"Untrained NVE>1.5×\", \"Max NVE (trained)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"5/5\", \"0/7\", \"4.12×\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"3/3\", \"0/5\", \"70.64×\"]\n          - [\"PickCube\", \"1/1\", \"—\", \"3.78×\"]\n          - [\"**Total**\", \"**9/9**\", \"**0/12**\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot: NVE distributions by condition (trained vs untrained) across environments\"\n    analysis: >\n      NVE 诊断方法的 cross-environment robustness confirmation。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":752,"cache_read_input_tokens":90026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":752},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"68097478-cbd2-4644-b420-2113bd7d1c88","uuid":"1b9d06ee-a3f5-44f1-8cb8-8afadb502814"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":596438,"duration_api_ms":598166,"num_turns":5,"result":"All planned experiments identified. Now generating the best-tier predictions with full rationale for each.\n\n```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 framing 完全成立。论文以 \"Diagnostic Analysis of Value Overestimation from Temporal\n  Abstraction in DreamerV3\" 被接受为高质量诊断论文。三重贡献被认可：\n  (1) CIVO 因果链 (trained dt_emb → RSSM fidelity gap → value overestimation → actor exploitation)\n  配合 NVE≥1.5× 诊断标记 (AUROC 0.969)；\n  (2) MPC vs imagination 架构边界 — TAWM 在 MPC 成功但 dt-conditioning 在 imagination-based AC\n  失败，定位 critic bootstrapping 为特定脆弱点（genuinely novel）；\n  (3) Intervention Hierarchy — 17 seeds × 7 methods × 3 levels 系统性评估，证明 CIVO 在\n  gradient/output/representation 三层均难可靠缓解（首次系统性评估）。\n  梯度大小 ≠ 因果重要性（reward 38-49% 梯度但 reward-only SGS 失败最惨；obs-decoder 16-22%\n  但因果关键）被视为超越本文的可迁移方法论洞察。\n  Countermeasures 讨论成功 preempt R9（Double Q 需重构 255-bin categorical critic；MBPO\n  truncation 无法解决 single-step reward bias；ensemble critics 定位为最有前景 future work）。\n  NVE 诊断 AUROC=0.969 配合 Youden-optimal 独立收敛至 1.53× 的说明，化解 in-sample 质疑。\n  Pixel obs 定位为明确 limitation + future work，proprioceptive 设定为 controlled baseline。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # GROUP 1: Walker Walk Multi-Seed Replication\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: >\n      复现 CIVO collapse 的多 seed 验证。008d 配置 (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8)。\n      Registry 已完成: 009e (s1) + 009b (s2)。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 131.08\n      seed1_nve_peak: 4.12\n      seed1_nve_peak_step: 55000\n      seed1_collapse: true\n      seed1_collapse_type: \"classic_CIVO_value_driven\"\n      seed2_eval_105K: 267.93\n      seed2_nve_peak: 2.05\n      seed2_nve_peak_step: 25000\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed2_self_correction: true\n      seed2_nve_final: 0.38\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x: \"2/2\"\n      cross_seed_collapse_rate: \"1/2\"\n      independent_collapse_rate: \"1/2 (008d s0 与 009e s1 共享 seed=1, 视为同一观测)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, 2/2 trained dt_emb seeds 均超过 NVE 1.5× 被接受为 CIVO 诊断标记的\n      强 supporting evidence。审稿人理解 collapse 是 stochastic 的——关键发现不是\n      \"必然崩溃\" 而是 \"trained dt_emb 可靠触发病态过估值 (NVE>1.5×)\"。\n      Seed 1 的经典 CIVO (value-driven, entropy ↓, NVE 1.78→2.09→4.12 加速) vs\n      Seed 2 的自我修正 (NVE 2.05→1.62→0.38 衰减) 被视为丰富了 CIVO 动态的理解，\n      而非削弱了 claim。Sustained vs transient NVE>1.5× 的差异性（seed 1 连续3个\n      checkpoint 维持>1.5× → 不可逆; seed 2 仅一次突破 → 自我修正）与 Henderson\n      et al. 2018 的早期随机性影响结论一致。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Walker 008d Cross-Seed Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE_peak\", \"NVE_peak_step\", \"Collapse?\", \"Pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0 (008d)\", \"82.75\", \"4.12\", \"55K\", \"Yes\", \"Value-driven, entropy ↓\"]\n          - [\"s1 (009e)\", \"131.08\", \"4.12\", \"55K\", \"Yes\", \"Same seed as s0, deterministic replication\"]\n          - [\"s2 (009b)\", \"267.93\", \"2.05\", \"25K\", \"No\", \"Transient NVE → self-correction\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Learning curves (eval + NVE) for 008d s0/s1/s2 overlaid, showing divergence point at ~35K\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 核心证据：trained dt_emb 可靠触发 NVE>1.5× (2/2 independent seeds)。\n      Collapse 是 stochastic (1/2)，但 diagnostic marker 是 deterministic。\n      Best 档审稿人接受这一区分，不要求 deterministic collapse。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: >\n      C2 因果控制的多 seed 验证。008f 配置 (dt=2, subsample ON, dt_embed_dim=0, H=8)。\n      Registry: 009f (s1) killed → 使用替代 seeds (008f_s3, 008f_s4); 009c (s2) done。\n    expected_results:\n      seed2_eval_105K: 148.34\n      seed2_nve_peak: 1.26\n      seed2_nve_105K: 1.14\n      seed2_collapse: false\n      seed3_eval_105K: 363.8\n      seed3_nve_peak: \"<1.5x\"\n      seed3_collapse: false\n      seed4_eval_105K: 306.5\n      seed4_nve_peak: 1.41\n      seed4_nve_105K: 0.58\n      seed4_collapse: false\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x: \"0/3\"\n      reward_MAE_baseline_ratio: \"~75x\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, 0/3 seeds 超过 NVE 1.5× 被接受为 dt_embedding 因果控制的决定性证据。\n      与 008d 的 2/2 形成 5/5 完美分离（trained 2/2 exceed, untrained 0/3 never exceed）。\n      审稿人注意到 009c 的 NVE=1.14@105K 接近但未达 1.5× threshold，且 008f_s4 的\n      transient NVE=1.41@85K 也在 threshold 以下——threshold 的区分力成立。\n      008f reward_MAE=0.747（baseline 75×）是已知 trade-off: 去掉 dt_embedding 后 reward\n      head 无法区分 dt=1/dt=2。审稿人接受这不削弱因果结论——因果控制实验证明的是\n      \"去掉 X → 无崩溃\"，不需要 reward 预测同样好。R8 被 preempt。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 008f Causal Control Cross-Seed\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE_peak\", \"NVE@105K\", \"CIVO?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0 (008f)\", \"503\", \"1.02\", \"0.30\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"s2 (009c)\", \"148.34\", \"1.26\", \"1.14\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"s3\", \"363.8\", \"<1.5\", \"—\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"s4\", \"306.5\", \"1.41\", \"0.58\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"NVE trajectories: 008d seeds (red, above 1.5× line) vs 008f seeds (blue, below 1.5× line)\"\n    analysis: >\n      与 008d 2/2 对比，形成 trained vs untrained dt_emb 的完美二分类。\n      Best 档审稿人视 008f 为 \"definitive causal control\"，008f 的低 eval 被理解为\n      因果控制实验的预期代价。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: >\n      C3 value growth suppression 多 seed 验证。008a 配置 (dt=2, subsample OFF, trained\n      dt_emb unexposed to dt>1 data, H=15)。Registry 已完成: 008a_unexposed_s1, s2。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 630.91\n      seed1_ve_ratio_105K: 0.43\n      seed1_civo_alert: 0\n      seed1_delta_ve: -0.0028\n      seed2_eval_105K: 899.4\n      seed2_ve_ratio_105K: 0.333\n      seed2_civo_alert: 0\n      seed2_delta_ve: -0.003\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x: \"0/2\"\n      cross_seed_eval_mean: 765.2\n      cross_seed_eval_range: \"631-899\"\n      vs_baseline_mean: \"83.5%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, unexposed dt_emb（trained 但训练数据中无 dt>1 transition）的两个新 seed\n      均展现 value suppression + 无 CIVO。Seed 2 特别强 (899.4 = 98% baseline)。\n      Cross-seed 均值 765 (83.5% baseline) 显著优于 008f (均值 ~330, 36% baseline)。\n      审稿人将此解读为: 真正有害的不是 dt_embedding 本身的存在，而是当 training data\n      中含有 dt>1 transitions 时 dt_embedding 学到 dt-specific representations。\n      这强化了 C2 的机制性解释（RSSM fidelity gap + learned conditioning amplification），\n      而非简单的 \"有 dt_emb = 坏\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 008a Unexposed Cross-Seed\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"VE ratio@105K\", \"NVE@105K\", \"Pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0 (008a)\", \"777.66\", \"0.386\", \"0.59\", \"Zigzag recovery, 2 V-cycles\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"630.91\", \"0.43\", \"~0.65\", \"Rising trend\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"899.4\", \"0.333\", \"~0.51\", \"Strong convergence, near-baseline\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Learning curves: 008a 3 seeds vs baseline band, showing zigzag recovery pattern\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3 核心证据加强。3 seeds 一致展现 value suppression (NVE 0.51-0.65x)。\n      高 seed variance (631-899) 被理解为 dt>1 数据缺失导致的学习不稳定，\n      而非方法论缺陷。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (dt=1 imagination) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: >\n      C6 dt=1 imagination 效果验证。008e_v3 配置 (trained dt_emb, dt=1 imagination, subsample\n      ON, H=15)。Registry 已完成: s1 (success), s2 (collapsed non-CIVO)。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_105K: 869.88\n      seed1_nve_peak: 0.80\n      seed1_ve_ratio_105K: 0.527\n      seed1_collapse: false\n      seed1_gate_dt_1_frac: 1.0\n      seed2_eval_105K: 136.96\n      seed2_nve_peak: 3.78\n      seed2_nve_105K: 3.78\n      seed2_collapse: true\n      seed2_collapse_onset: \"95K\"\n      seed2_actor_entropy_trend: \"rising (-5.21@85K → -3.83@105K)\"\n      seed2_gate_dt_1_frac: 1.0\n      cross_seed_collapse_rate: \"1/2\"\n      collapse_mechanism_difference: \"seed2 = eval-driven (Pathway B), not value-driven (Pathway A)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, C6 PARTIALLY FALSIFIED 被透明报告并获审稿人认可。dt=1 imagination\n      不能阻止崩溃 (1/2 seeds)，但崩溃机制与经典 CIVO 定性不同：\n      - 008d s0 (Pathway A): value 爆炸 → actor exploit → eval 下跌，entropy ↓\n      - 008e_v3 s2 (Pathway B): eval 先跌 → NVE 被动升高，entropy ↑ (策略变随机)\n      审稿人接受 \"trained dt_embedding creates vulnerability through multiple pathways\"\n      这一更深层洞察。009a baseline s2 在同期完全稳定 (618→596→836)，排除 seed\n      脆弱假说。这实际上丰富了论文贡献——CIVO 不是唯一的脆弱通道。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Pathway A vs Pathway B Collapse Dynamics\"\n        columns: [\"Feature\", \"008d s0 (Pathway A)\", \"008e_v3 s2 (Pathway B)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Value change\", \"Explosive (60→138, +130%@55K)\", \"Moderate (339→384→340, +13%→-12%)\"]\n          - [\"Eval change\", \"Post-value (146→83, -43%)\", \"Leads (715→452→137, -81%)\"]\n          - [\"NVE driver\", \"Value numerator (value explosion)\", \"Eval denominator (eval crash)\"]\n          - [\"Actor entropy\", \"↓ (-3.47→-4.88, policy locks)\", \"↑ (-5.21→-3.83, policy destabilizes)\"]\n          - [\"Mechanism\", \"Critic overestimate → actor exploit\", \"Eval crash → value lag\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-axis plot: value + entropy trajectories for Pathway A and B, color-coded\"\n    analysis: >\n      C6 从 \"practical mitigation\" 降级为 \"mechanistic insight: trained dt_emb 创建\n      多条脆弱通道\"。Best 档审稿人视此为 honest reporting + deeper understanding，\n      而非 weakness。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk FROZEN dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=2 imag + H=8\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: >\n      诊断 dt_emb TRAINING 是否为 CIVO 必要条件。dt_embedding 保持随机初始化但 freeze\n      (requires_grad=False)。Registry 已完成: exp_015b。\n    expected_results:\n      eval_105K: 204.2\n      nve_85K: 0.467\n      nve_95K: 0.394\n      nve_105K: 0.42\n      collapse: false\n      actor_loss_105K: 0.000179\n      actor_entropy_105K: -4.855\n      value_mean_105K: 56.212\n      gate_dt_mean: 2.0\n      collapse_mechanism: \"gradient_starvation_from_frozen_dt_emb\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, frozen dt_emb 不崩溃但性能很差 (204 = 22% baseline)。NVE 全程 0.39-0.47\n      (远低于 1.0×, critic 严重低估)，actor_loss → 0（梯度饥饿）。这确认了 dt_emb\n      的 TRAINING 是 CIVO 的必要条件——没有训练的 dt_embedding 只是噪声输入，\n      不会创建 RSSM 对精确 dt 信号的 co-adaptation。但 frozen embedding 引入了\n      新问题（梯度饥饿），证明这不是一个可行的 mitigation 方向。\n      审稿人将此视为 2×2 消融矩阵 (008a/008d/008f/015b) 的完成：\n      - 008d (trained + subsample ON): CIVO ✓\n      - 008a (trained + subsample OFF): No CIVO ✓ (unexposed)\n      - 008f (removed, subsample ON): No CIVO ✓ (no embedding)\n      - 015b (frozen + subsample ON): No CIVO ✓ (frozen)\n      只有 008d (trained AND exposed to dt>1 data) 产生 CIVO → training 是必要条件。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: dt_emb 2×2 Ablation Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"dt_emb state\", \"Exposed to dt>1?\", \"CIVO?\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE range\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"008d\", \"Trained\", \"Yes (subsample ON)\", \"Yes (2/2)\", \"82-131\", \"1.71-4.12\"]\n          - [\"008a\", \"Trained\", \"No (subsample OFF)\", \"No (0/3)\", \"631-899\", \"0.51-0.65\"]\n          - [\"008f\", \"Removed (dim=0)\", \"Yes\", \"No (0/4)\", \"148-503\", \"0.30-1.41\"]\n          - [\"015b\", \"Frozen (random init)\", \"Yes\", \"No (0/1)\", \"204\", \"0.39-0.47\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 grid: eval trajectories for each ablation cell\"\n    analysis: >\n      闭合因果推理: dt_emb training + exposure to dt>1 data 两个条件同时满足时才触发 CIVO。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 additional seeds (seed 3-4)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_016\"\n    description: >\n      缩小 008e_v3 (dt=1 imagination) 崩溃概率估计区间。Registry 已完成: s3 + s4。\n    expected_results:\n      seed3_eval_105K: 92.7\n      seed3_nve_peak: 4.02\n      seed3_collapse: true\n      seed3_collapse_onset: \"85K-95K\"\n      seed3_actor_entropy_final: -4.892\n      seed4_eval_105K: 899.3\n      seed4_nve_peak: 0.99\n      seed4_collapse: false\n      total_008e_v3_collapse_rate: \"2/4 (50%)\"\n      collapse_pathway_breakdown: \"s2 = Pathway B (eval-driven, entropy ↑); s3 = mixed (entropy remains low)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, 2/4 崩溃率 (50%) 与 008d 的 1/2 (50%) 完全一致——dt=1 imagination\n      未降低崩溃概率。这是 C6 PARTIALLY FALSIFIED 的最有力量化证据。\n      s3 崩溃 (NVE 4.02, entropy stays low at -4.892) 引入了第三种可能的动态模式，\n      但 best 档审稿人不要求对每个 seed 的机制差异做完整解释——4 seeds 确认 50%\n      崩溃率已经足够。核心结论: trained dt_embedding 是根本脆弱源，dt=1 imagination\n      只消除了一条特定通道 (Pathway A) 但不消除全部通道。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: 008e_v3 Cross-Seed Summary (dt=1 imagination)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE_peak\", \"Collapse?\", \"Pathway\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s1 (008e_v3)\", \"869.9\", \"0.80\", \"No\", \"Healthy\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"137.0\", \"3.78\", \"Yes\", \"B (eval-driven, entropy ↑)\"]\n          - [\"s3\", \"92.7\", \"4.02\", \"Yes\", \"Mixed (entropy stays low)\"]\n          - [\"s4\", \"899.3\", \"0.99\", \"No\", \"Healthy\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-seed eval trajectories with collapse markers, showing 50% divergence\"\n    analysis: >\n      50% collapse rate 确认 dt=1 imagination 非有效 mitigation。Best 档审稿人\n      视此为诚实报告 + 对 trained dt_emb 多通道脆弱性的系统性证据。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # GROUP 2: Cheetah Run Cross-Environment Validation\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: >\n      第二 DMC 环境基准线。Registry 已有 5 seeds (023a/023b/023_s2/s3/s4)。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_final: 624.7\n      seed1_eval_final: 520.3\n      seed2_eval_final: 645.4\n      seed3_eval_final: 642.13\n      seed4_eval_final: 537.03\n      cross_seed_mean: 593.9\n      cross_seed_std: 56.8\n      cross_seed_range: \"520-645\"\n      ve_ratio_converged: \"0.65-0.70\"\n      ve_ratio_stable_from: \"150K+\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Cheetah baseline 提供了 NVE 归一化的可靠分母。5 seeds 的一致性\n      (std=56.8, CV=9.6%) 表明 Cheetah 环境有适度但可接受的 seed variance。\n      VE ratio 收敛到 0.65-0.70 (类似 Walker 的 0.69-0.72)，支持 NVE 归一化方法\n      在跨环境的适用性。审稿人接受 5 seeds 足够建立可靠 baseline。\n      s4 的 194K→204K eval 骤降 (537→302) 被确认为 transient fluctuation\n      (延长到 300K 恢复到 642)，不是 instability。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cheetah Baseline Cross-Seed\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval final\", \"Peak eval\", \"VE ratio converged\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"624.7\", \"624.7\", \"~0.67\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"520.3\", \"572.9\", \"~0.65\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"645.4\", \"645.4\", \"~0.68\"]\n          - [\"s3\", \"642.1\", \"685.9\", \"~0.69\"]\n          - [\"s4\", \"537.0 (ext→642)\", \"642.3\", \"~0.66\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah baseline 5-seed learning curves with IQM band\"\n    analysis: >\n      Robust baseline。Cross-seed IQM ~600，用于所有 Cheetah CIVO 实验的归一化。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: >\n      Cheetah 环境 CIVO 复现。Registry: 010b (s1 eval 51.7, NVE 8.27) + 010b_s0\n      (eval 0.83, NVE 70.64)。需 seed 2 预测。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_final: 0.83\n      seed0_nve_peak: 70.64\n      seed0_collapse: true\n      seed1_eval_final: 51.7\n      seed1_nve_peak: 8.27\n      seed1_collapse: true\n      seed2_eval_final_predicted: 38.5\n      seed2_nve_peak_predicted: 12.4\n      seed2_nve_peak_step_predicted: \"55K\"\n      seed2_collapse_predicted: true\n      cross_seed_collapse_rate: \"3/3\"\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x: \"3/3\"\n      cheetah_vs_walker_severity: \"Cheetah NVE peaks 2-9× higher than Walker (8-70× vs 2-4×)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Cheetah CIVO 比 Walker 更严重但 100% 一致。Cheetah 的 3/3 崩溃率\n      (vs Walker 的 ~50%) 表明环境复杂度放大了 CIVO——更复杂的 dynamics → 更大的\n      RSSM fidelity gap → 更强的 value overestimation feedback loop。\n      NVE peaks 远高于 Walker (8-70× vs 2-4×) 同样支持这一解读。\n      审稿人将跨环境 NVE severity 差异视为支持 \"CIVO severity scales with RSSM prediction\n      difficulty\" 的证据——这不是 noise，而是 signal。\n      Seed 2 预测基于 s0/s1 的模式: Cheetah 中 CIVO 更可靠 (100% vs Walker 50%)，\n      NVE peak 在 8-70× 范围内。保守预测 12.4× 处于该范围中段。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cheetah CIVO Trigger Cross-Seed\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval final\", \"NVE_peak\", \"Collapse?\", \"Baseline%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"0.83\", \"70.64\", \"Yes\", \"0.1%\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"51.7\", \"8.27\", \"Yes\", \"8.7%\"]\n          - [\"s2 (predicted)\", \"38.5\", \"12.4\", \"Yes\", \"6.5%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah CIVO: NVE trajectories showing extreme overestimation peaks\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cheetah 100% collapse rate 加强了 C1 + C2。与 Walker 的 severity 差异\n      提供了额外的 mechanistic insight。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: >\n      Cheetah 因果控制。Registry: 024b_s0 (eval 96.5, no CIVO), 024b_s1 (eval 77.3).\n      Need seed 2 prediction.\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_final: 96.5\n      seed0_nve_peak: 0.2\n      seed0_civo: false\n      seed1_eval_final: 77.3\n      seed1_nve_peak: 0.1\n      seed1_civo: false\n      seed2_eval_final_predicted: 88.2\n      seed2_nve_peak_predicted: 0.15\n      seed2_civo_predicted: false\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x: \"0/3\"\n      cross_seed_eval_mean: 87.3\n      vs_baseline: \"14.7%\"\n      reward_prediction_quality: \"severely degraded (similar to Walker 008f pattern)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Cheetah no-dt-emb 完美复现 Walker 008f 的模式: 0/3 CIVO, 但 eval\n      严重下降 (14.7% baseline)。NVE 全程极低 (<0.2×)，连 baseline 水平的 value\n      估计都无法达到。这不是好的 mitigation (性能损失太大)，但作为因果控制完美:\n      去掉 dt_embedding → CIVO 消失。\n      Cheetah 的 dt-emb-removal 性能损失 (14.7%) 比 Walker (36%) 更大，这合理——\n      Cheetah 的更复杂 dynamics 意味着缺失 temporal information 的代价更高。\n      审稿人接受 008f/024b 是因果控制而非推荐方案。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cheetah Causal Control (no dt_emb)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval final\", \"NVE_peak\", \"CIVO?\", \"Baseline%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"96.5\", \"0.2\", \"No\", \"15.4%\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"77.3\", \"0.1\", \"No\", \"12.3%\"]\n          - [\"s2 (predicted)\", \"88.2\", \"0.15\", \"No\", \"14.8%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah: CIVO trigger (red) vs no-dt-emb control (blue) eval curves\"\n    analysis: >\n      跨环境因果控制复现。dt_embedding removal 的 5/5 (Walker) + 3/3 (Cheetah) = 8/8\n      CIVO prevention rate。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: >\n      Cheetah unexposed dt_emb 验证 (C3)。Registry: 008a_cheetah_s0 (532.35, NVE 0.49),\n      s1 (504.38, NVE 0.478). Need seed 2 prediction.\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K: 532.35\n      seed0_nve_105K: 0.49\n      seed0_civo: false\n      seed1_eval_105K: 504.38\n      seed1_nve_105K: 0.478\n      seed1_civo: false\n      seed2_eval_105K_predicted: 518.6\n      seed2_nve_105K_predicted: 0.48\n      seed2_civo_predicted: false\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x: \"0/3\"\n      cross_seed_eval_mean: 518.4\n      vs_baseline: \"87.3%\"\n      vs_no_dt_emb: \"5.9x better (518 vs 87)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Cheetah unexposed dt_emb 展现出与 Walker 008a 一致的 pattern:\n      接近 baseline 的性能 (87% vs Walker 83.5%), NVE 全程受抑 (0.48-0.49×),\n      无 CIVO。这与 no-dt-emb (plan_022, 14.7% baseline) 形成鲜明对比——\n      保留 dt_embedding 但不暴露于 dt>1 data 是明显更优的方案。\n      跨环境一致性极高 (Walker 83.5% vs Cheetah 87.3% of baseline)，审稿人将此\n      视为 C3 在第二环境的强复现。Seed variance 在 Cheetah 很小 (504-532, 2.7%)\n      vs Walker 的较大 variance (631-899, 17.4%)——可能因为 Cheetah 的 simpler\n      reward structure 导致更一致的学习。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cheetah Unexposed dt_emb (C3 validation)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE@105K\", \"CIVO?\", \"Baseline%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"532.4\", \"0.49\", \"No\", \"89.7%\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"504.4\", \"0.48\", \"No\", \"84.9%\"]\n          - [\"s2 (predicted)\", \"518.6\", \"0.48\", \"No\", \"87.3%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment C3 comparison: Walker 008a vs Cheetah unexposed, normalized\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3 跨环境验证完成。Unexposed dt_emb 在两环境均提供 >83% baseline 性能和 NVE<0.5×。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # GROUP 3: Cartpole Swingup (Non-Locomotion Validation)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: >\n      非运动型 DMC 环境基准线。DreamerV3 proprioceptive Cartpole Swingup。\n      全部为预测数据。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_final_predicted: 842.3\n      seed1_eval_final_predicted: 818.6\n      seed2_eval_final_predicted: 854.1\n      cross_seed_mean_predicted: 838.3\n      cross_seed_std_predicted: 18.0\n      convergence_step_predicted: \"~80K (faster than Walker ~100K due to simpler dynamics)\"\n      ve_ratio_converged_predicted: \"0.68-0.73\"\n      eval_peak_range_predicted: \"850-870\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Cartpole Swingup baseline 提供非运动环境的参考点。DreamerV3 在\n      proprioceptive Cartpole 上通常达到 ~830-860 (基于公开 benchmark)。\n      收敛更快 (~80K vs Walker ~100K) 因为 observation space 更小 (5D vs 24D)\n      且 dynamics 更简单。VE ratio 收敛到类似 Walker/Cheetah 的 ~0.70 范围，\n      表明 DreamerV3 的 value calibration 跨环境一致。\n      低 seed variance (CV ~2.1%) 预期因为 Cartpole 的 simpler dynamics 导致\n      更一致的学习。审稿人接受这作为第三环境 baseline。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cartpole Swingup Baseline (predicted)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval final\", \"VE ratio\", \"Convergence step\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"842.3\", \"0.71\", \"~78K\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"818.6\", \"0.69\", \"~82K\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"854.1\", \"0.73\", \"~76K\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole baseline learning curves with Walker/Cheetah normalized comparison\"\n    analysis: >\n      非运动环境 baseline 确立。对 C1/C2/C3 的跨 task-type 验证至关重要。\n      但 best 档 narrative 指出 Walker+Cheetah+PickCube 已足够——Cartpole\n      是 additional strength, not a requirement。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: >\n      非运动环境 CIVO 复现。全部为预测数据。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K_predicted: 127.4\n      seed0_nve_peak_predicted: 3.21\n      seed0_nve_peak_step_predicted: \"55K\"\n      seed0_collapse_predicted: true\n      seed1_eval_105K_predicted: 612.7\n      seed1_nve_peak_predicted: 1.83\n      seed1_nve_peak_step_predicted: \"45K\"\n      seed1_collapse_predicted: false\n      seed1_self_correction_predicted: true\n      seed2_eval_105K_predicted: 95.6\n      seed2_nve_peak_predicted: 4.47\n      seed2_nve_peak_step_predicted: \"65K\"\n      seed2_collapse_predicted: true\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x_predicted: \"3/3\"\n      cross_seed_collapse_rate_predicted: \"2/3\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Cartpole CIVO 表现与 Walker 类似而非 Cheetah。Cartpole 的简单\n      dynamics 意味着 RSSM fidelity gap 中等 (类似 Walker)，所以 CIVO severity\n      处于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间。3/3 seeds 超过 NVE 1.5× (诊断标记一致),\n      2/3 collapse (类似 Walker 50% rate)。\n      Seed 1 自我修正模式与 009b (Walker) 一致——transient NVE>1.5× 后衰减。\n      这跨环境复现了 \"sustained vs transient NVE\" 的 stochastic divergence 模式。\n      审稿人将此视为 CIVO 机制跨 task type 的强验证——不仅限于 locomotion。\n      NVE peaks (1.83-4.47) 处于 Walker (2.05-4.12) 类似范围，而非 Cheetah 的\n      极端范围 (8-70×)，支持 \"CIVO severity ~ RSSM difficulty\" 假设。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cartpole CIVO Trigger (predicted)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE_peak\", \"Collapse?\", \"Pattern\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"127.4\", \"3.21\", \"Yes\", \"Classic CIVO\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"612.7\", \"1.83\", \"No\", \"Transient → self-correction\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"95.6\", \"4.47\", \"Yes\", \"Classic CIVO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment NVE peak comparison: Walker / Cheetah / Cartpole\"\n    analysis: >\n      非运动环境 CIVO 确认。3/3 NVE>1.5× + 2/3 collapse, 与 locomotion 一致。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: >\n      非运动环境因果控制。全部为预测数据。\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_105K_predicted: 312.4\n      seed0_nve_peak_predicted: 0.35\n      seed0_civo_predicted: false\n      seed1_eval_105K_predicted: 278.9\n      seed1_nve_peak_predicted: 0.42\n      seed1_civo_predicted: false\n      seed2_eval_105K_predicted: 335.1\n      seed2_nve_peak_predicted: 0.28\n      seed2_civo_predicted: false\n      cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x_predicted: \"0/3\"\n      cross_seed_eval_mean_predicted: 308.8\n      vs_baseline_predicted: \"36.8%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Cartpole no-dt-emb 复现 Walker/Cheetah 的因果控制模式:\n      0/3 CIVO, eval 显著低于 baseline (36.8%)。\n      Cartpole 的 eval loss (63.2%) 介于 Walker (64%) 和 Cheetah (85.3%) 之间，\n      与环境复杂度的排序一致 (Cheetah > Cartpole > Walker in temporal info value)。\n      但这可能存在混淆 (Cartpole 的 temporal info 可能天然不如 locomotion 重要)，\n      best 档审稿人不深究此点——关键是 CIVO prevention = 100%。\n      跨三环境汇总: dt_emb removal → 0/11 CIVO (Walker 0/4 + Cheetah 0/3 + Cartpole 0/3 + PickCube 0/1)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cartpole Causal Control (predicted)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Eval@105K\", \"NVE_peak\", \"CIVO?\", \"Baseline%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"s0\", \"312.4\", \"0.35\", \"No\", \"37.1%\"]\n          - [\"s1\", \"278.9\", \"0.42\", \"No\", \"33.1%\"]\n          - [\"s2\", \"335.1\", \"0.28\", \"No\", \"39.9%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment causal control summary bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      第三环境因果控制完成。dt_emb removal → 0/11 CIVO prevention 跨所有环境。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # GROUP 4: Analysis Tasks (0-1 GPU hours)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: >\n      RSSM fidelity gap 量化。Registry 已完成: exp_rssm_fidelity_analysis。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_dt1_obs_MSE: 13.49\n      baseline_dt2_obs_MSE: 27.50\n      baseline_obs_gap: 2.04\n      baseline_dt1_reward_MAE: 0.0102\n      baseline_dt2_reward_MAE: 0.0159\n      baseline_reward_gap: 1.56\n      008d_dt1_obs_MSE: 41.31\n      008d_dt2_obs_MSE: 53.67\n      008d_obs_gap: 1.30\n      008d_dt1_reward_MAE: 0.0568\n      008d_dt2_reward_MAE: 0.1579\n      008d_reward_gap: 2.78\n      008f_dt1_obs_MSE: 8.01\n      008f_dt2_obs_MSE: 22.04\n      008f_obs_gap: 2.75\n      008f_dt1_reward_MAE: 0.7469\n      008f_dt2_reward_MAE: 0.7526\n      008f_reward_gap: 1.01\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, RSSM fidelity 表是 C2 机制解释的核心定量支撑。关键 insight:\n      (1) 008d obs_gap 仅 1.30× (看似小), 但 dt1 绝对误差 41.31 已是 baseline 的 3×\n      → 模型本身已崩塌，低 gap ratio 是误导性的。论文必须并排呈现绝对值和比率。\n      (2) 008d reward_gap 2.78× → trained dt_emb 让 reward head 学到了精确的\n      dt-specific reward predictions, 但这个精确度建立在 RSSM 的 imprecise states 上\n      → 系统性 reward 过估。\n      (3) 008f reward_gap 1.01× → no dt_emb 时 reward head 完全无法区分 dt=1/dt=2,\n      reward_MAE=0.747 (baseline 75×), 这是 \"去掉 dt_emb 代价太大\" 的定量证据。\n      审稿人视此表为 \"smoking gun\"——不是模型不好，而是 conditioning 让模型在错误的\n      基础上过于 confident。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1 (论文): RSSM Fidelity Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"dt1 obs_MSE\", \"dt2 obs_MSE\", \"obs gap\", \"dt1 rew_MAE\", \"dt2 rew_MAE\", \"rew gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline (dt=1)\", \"13.49\", \"27.50\", \"2.04×\", \"0.010\", \"0.016\", \"1.56×\"]\n          - [\"008d (trained dt_emb)\", \"41.31\", \"53.67\", \"1.30×*\", \"0.057\", \"0.158\", \"2.78×\"]\n          - [\"008f (no dt_emb)\", \"8.01\", \"22.04\", \"2.75×\", \"0.747\", \"0.753\", \"1.01×\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: absolute errors (grouped by model) + ratio annotations\"\n      - \"* 008d low obs gap ratio is misleading — absolute errors are 3× baseline\"\n    analysis: >\n      Figure 4 / Table 1 核心证据。三模型对比完整揭示 trained dt_emb 如何创建\n      CIVO 的 forward-pass 基础。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: >\n      从现有 metrics.jsonl 提取 actor_entropy trajectories。0 GPU cost。\n    expected_results:\n      008d_s0_entropy_35K: -3.465\n      008d_s0_entropy_45K: -4.575\n      008d_s0_entropy_55K: -4.879\n      008d_s0_trend: \"monotonic decrease → policy locks onto overestimated actions\"\n      008e_v3_s2_entropy_85K: -5.208\n      008e_v3_s2_entropy_95K: -4.529\n      008e_v3_s2_entropy_105K: -3.828\n      008e_v3_s2_trend: \"increase during collapse → policy destabilizes\"\n      008a_s0_entropy_105K_predicted: -5.1\n      008a_s0_trend: \"stable convergence to low entropy (normal learning)\"\n      baseline_entropy_converged_predicted: \"-5.2 to -5.5\"\n      016e_entropy_comparison: \"SGS preserves ~1.0-1.3 nats higher entropy through 35-55K\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, actor entropy 分析提供了 Pathway A vs B 的独立定量区分。\n      Pathway A (008d s0): entropy 单调下降 (-3.47 → -4.88) = actor 变得越来越\n      deterministic，exploit overestimated value regions。这是经典 CIVO 签名。\n      Pathway B (008e_v3 s2): entropy 上升 (-5.21 → -3.83) = policy 在崩溃期间\n      变随机，失去已学结构。这与 value-driven exploitation 相反。\n      健康配置 (008a, baseline): entropy 稳定收敛到 ~-5.2 (正常确定性策略)。\n      SGS (016e) 的高 entropy (+1.0-1.3 nats) 解释了它为何延迟但不阻止 CIVO:\n      更多探索暂时抵消了 value overestimation, 但无法永久阻止。\n      审稿人视此为 Figure 级别的 supporting evidence, 加强了论文的机制性叙事。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Actor Entropy Signatures\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"Entropy@35K\", \"Entropy@55K\", \"Entropy@105K\", \"Trend\", \"Classification\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline s0\", \"-4.2\", \"-5.0\", \"-5.3\", \"Converging ↓\", \"Healthy\"]\n          - [\"008a s0 (unexposed)\", \"-3.8\", \"-4.6\", \"-5.1\", \"Converging ↓\", \"Healthy\"]\n          - [\"008d s0 (CIVO)\", \"-3.47\", \"-4.88\", \"—(collapsed)\", \"Accelerating ↓\", \"Pathway A\"]\n          - [\"008e_v3 s2\", \"-5.12\", \"-5.12\", \"-3.83\", \"Rising ↑ at collapse\", \"Pathway B\"]\n          - [\"016e (SGS)\", \"-2.12\", \"-3.62\", \"—(collapsed)\", \"Delayed ↓\", \"SGS-modified CIVO\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure: Entropy trajectories — healthy (blue) vs Pathway A (red) vs Pathway B (orange)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Entropy 分析提供了 collapse 动态的独立验证维度。Best 档审稿人将此\n      视为 mechanism-level claim 的有力 supplementary evidence。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: >\n      V(s) vs Monte Carlo return 分布对比。1 GPU hour for trajectory collection。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_v_mc_correlation_predicted: 0.92\n      baseline_v_mc_bias_predicted: \"+2-5% (slight optimism, normal)\"\n      008d_v_mc_correlation_35K_predicted: 0.71\n      008d_v_mc_correlation_55K_predicted: 0.38\n      008d_v_mc_bias_55K_predicted: \"+180% (extreme optimism at dt>1 states)\"\n      008d_dt2_specific_bias_predicted: \"+250% at dt=2 imagined states vs +40% at dt=1\"\n      008a_v_mc_correlation_predicted: 0.85\n      008a_v_mc_bias_predicted: \"-5% (slight pessimism, consistent with NVE<1.0×)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, distributional analysis 升级了 v/e ratio proxy 的说服力。\n      关键发现: 008d 的 value overestimation 不是 uniform 的——它集中在 dt>1\n      imagined states (+250%), 而 dt=1 states 仅有 +40% 偏差。这直接证明了\n      trained dt_embedding + RSSM fidelity gap 的交互效应。\n      008a 的轻微 pessimism (-5%) 与 NVE<1.0× 一致，说明 unexposed dt_emb\n      实际上倾向于 underestimate value (safe bias)。\n      审稿人视此为 \"beyond a crude proxy\" (preempt R3) 的关键补充分析。\n      如果时间不足, best 档 narrative 中 v/e ratio proxy 仍被接受 (R3 被 preempt\n      by the 4/4 NVE threshold + AUROC analysis)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: V(s) vs MC Return Statistics\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"V-MC correlation\", \"Mean bias\", \"dt>1 specific bias\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline\", \"0.92\", \"+3%\", \"N/A (dt=1 only)\"]\n          - [\"008d@35K\", \"0.71\", \"+85%\", \"+160% at dt=2\"]\n          - [\"008d@55K\", \"0.38\", \"+180%\", \"+250% at dt=2\"]\n          - [\"008a@105K\", \"0.85\", \"-5%\", \"N/A (unexposed)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plots: V(s) vs MC return, color-coded by dt, with regression lines\"\n    analysis: >\n      P2 优先级, 但若完成则显著加强 C2 的 mechanistic depth。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: >\n      跟踪 dt=1 和 dt=2 embedding vectors 在训练过程中的分离。0 GPU cost。\n    expected_results:\n      initial_cosine_sim_predicted: 0.02\n      cosine_sim_15K_predicted: -0.12\n      cosine_sim_35K_predicted: -0.38\n      cosine_sim_55K_predicted: -0.52\n      cosine_sim_105K_predicted: -0.61\n      embedding_norm_ratio_dt2_vs_dt1_predicted: 1.34\n      divergence_onset_predicted: \"10-15K (coincides with reward head learning dt-specific predictions)\"\n      frozen_cosine_sim_predicted: 0.02  # constant (frozen embedding)\n      008f_predicted: \"N/A (dt_embed_dim=0)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, embedding cosine similarity 提供了 trained dt_emb 如何 diverge 的\n      可视化证据。dt=1 和 dt=2 embeddings 从近似随机 (cos~0) 分化到显著负相关\n      (cos~-0.5 to -0.6)。分化 onset (~15K) 与 reward head 开始区分 dt=1/dt=2\n      的时间一致 (RSSM fidelity 表中 008d reward_gap 从 15K 开始明显 > 1.0)。\n      Embedding norm ratio >1 表明 dt=2 embedding 的幅度更大——可能因为 RSSM\n      需要更强的 conditioning signal 来处理较大的 temporal gap。\n      审稿人视此为 minor supplementary analysis。不会改变论文的核心评估，\n      但为 appendix/supplementary 提供了有用的可视化。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: dt_embedding Cosine Similarity Evolution\"\n        columns: [\"Step\", \"cos(emb_dt1, emb_dt2)\", \"||emb_dt2|| / ||emb_dt1||\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0 (init)\", \"0.02\", \"1.00\"]\n          - [\"15K\", \"-0.12\", \"1.08\"]\n          - [\"35K\", \"-0.38\", \"1.21\"]\n          - [\"55K\", \"-0.52\", \"1.30\"]\n          - [\"105K\", \"-0.61\", \"1.34\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: cosine similarity over training steps, annotated with CIVO onset\"\n    analysis: >\n      P2 supplementary analysis。Embedding divergence 与 CIVO onset 的时间相关性\n      提供了额外的 mechanistic link。\n\n  - name: \"NVE threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_034\"\n    description: >\n      从所有已完成实验计算 NVE 分类性能。0 GPU cost。AUROC + Youden-optimal threshold。\n    expected_results:\n      total_data_points: 29\n      environments: 4\n      AUROC: 0.969\n      threshold_sweep:\n        t1.0: {sensitivity: 1.00, specificity: 0.72, accuracy: 0.83, youden_J: 0.72}\n        t1.2: {sensitivity: 0.96, specificity: 0.86, accuracy: 0.90, youden_J: 0.82}\n        t1.3: {sensitivity: 0.93, specificity: 0.93, accuracy: 0.93, youden_J: 0.86}\n        t1.5: {sensitivity: 0.93, specificity: 0.97, accuracy: 0.95, youden_J: 0.90}\n        t1.7: {sensitivity: 0.86, specificity: 1.00, accuracy: 0.93, youden_J: 0.86}\n        t2.0: {sensitivity: 0.75, specificity: 1.00, accuracy: 0.88, youden_J: 0.75}\n      youden_optimal_threshold: 1.53\n      youden_optimal_J: 0.905\n      classification_at_1.5x:\n        true_positives: 13  # trained dt_emb seeds exceeding 1.5×\n        true_negatives: 14  # non-CIVO seeds never exceeding 1.5×\n        false_positives: 1  # non-CIVO seed transiently approaching 1.5× (borderline)\n        false_negatives: 1  # trained dt_emb seed briefly touching 1.5× but self-correcting before sustained\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, AUROC=0.969 配合 Youden-optimal 独立收敛到 1.53× 化解了 in-sample\n      calibration 质疑 (R10)。审稿人认可:\n      (1) Youden-optimal 1.53× 与预设 1.5× 的独立收敛不是 overfitting——如果 threshold\n      是 post-hoc 选择, Youden optimal 不太可能恰好落在同一位置。\n      (2) 4 环境 × 多 config 提供了 reasonable diversity, 尽管仍是 in-sample。\n      (3) 1-2 个 borderline cases (false positive/negative) 的存在反而增加可信度——\n      perfect 分类在小样本下更像 overfitting。\n      审稿人建议 held-out validation 作为 future work, 但不作为 major weakness。\n      NVE 在不同 reward scale 下的 generalization boundary 被明确讨论 (Cheetah NVE\n      peaks 远高于 Walker, 但 threshold 仍有效分类)。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: NVE Threshold Sensitivity (AUROC=0.969)\"\n        columns: [\"Threshold\", \"Sensitivity\", \"Specificity\", \"Accuracy\", \"Youden J\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1.0×\", \"1.00\", \"0.72\", \"0.83\", \"0.72\"]\n          - [\"1.2×\", \"0.96\", \"0.86\", \"0.90\", \"0.82\"]\n          - [\"1.3×\", \"0.93\", \"0.93\", \"0.93\", \"0.86\"]\n          - [\"**1.5×**\", \"**0.93**\", \"**0.97**\", \"**0.95**\", \"**0.90**\"]\n          - [\"1.7×\", \"0.86\", \"1.00\", \"0.93\", \"0.86\"]\n          - [\"2.0×\", \"0.75\", \"1.00\", \"0.88\", \"0.75\"]\n      - name: \"Table: Youden-Optimal Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"AUROC\", \"0.969\"]\n          - [\"Youden-optimal threshold\", \"1.53×\"]\n          - [\"Preselected threshold\", \"1.50×\"]\n          - [\"Convergence gap\", \"0.03× (2%)\"]\n          - [\"N data points\", \"29\"]\n          - [\"N environments\", \"4\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ROC curve with AUROC annotation and Youden-optimal point marked\"\n      - \"Threshold vs accuracy/sensitivity/specificity trade-off curves\"\n    analysis: >\n      NVE 诊断的定量基础。AUROC 0.969 + Youden 独立收敛是论文最强的方法论贡献之一。\n      Best 档审稿人接受 with caveat (in-sample), 不降级为 major weakness。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # GROUP 5: Hopper Hop + Exploratory\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: >\n      第三 locomotion 环境。P2 优先级。全部为预测数据。\n    expected_results:\n      baseline:\n        seed0_eval_final_predicted: 232.4\n        seed1_eval_final_predicted: 178.6\n        seed2_eval_final_predicted: 256.8\n        mean_predicted: 222.6\n        std_predicted: 40.1\n        ve_ratio_converged_predicted: \"0.55-0.65\"\n      civo_trigger:\n        seed0_eval_final_predicted: 45.3\n        seed0_nve_peak_predicted: 5.62\n        seed0_collapse_predicted: true\n        seed1_eval_final_predicted: 123.8\n        seed1_nve_peak_predicted: 2.31\n        seed1_collapse_predicted: false\n        seed2_eval_final_predicted: 31.7\n        seed2_nve_peak_predicted: 7.84\n        seed2_collapse_predicted: true\n        cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x_predicted: \"3/3\"\n        cross_seed_collapse_rate_predicted: \"2/3\"\n      no_dt_emb:\n        seed0_eval_final_predicted: 72.5\n        seed0_nve_peak_predicted: 0.31\n        seed1_eval_final_predicted: 58.3\n        seed1_nve_peak_predicted: 0.25\n        seed2_eval_final_predicted: 84.1\n        seed2_nve_peak_predicted: 0.38\n        cross_seed_nve_above_1.5x_predicted: \"0/3\"\n        vs_baseline_predicted: \"32.2%\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Hopper Hop 是 P2 额外验证——论文叙事不依赖它, 但若完成则强化\n      generalization claim。Hopper 是较难的 locomotion task (DreamerV3 baseline\n      ~180-260), seed variance 较大 (CV ~18%) 因为 hopping 任务对 policy\n      细微差异更敏感。\n      CIVO trigger 预测遵循 Walker 模式: 3/3 NVE>1.5×, 2/3 collapse。\n      NVE severity (2-8×) 介于 Walker (2-4×) 和 Cheetah (8-70×) 之间,\n      反映 Hopper dynamics 的中等复杂度。\n      No-dt-emb 预测 0/3 CIVO, eval ~32% baseline (类似 Walker/Cartpole)。\n      若完成, 跨环境 CIVO prevention 总计: Walker 0/4 + Cheetah 0/3 + PickCube 0/1\n      + Cartpole 0/3 + Hopper 0/3 = 0/14。\n      但 best 档审稿人已接受 3 环境足够——Hopper 是 bonus。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Hopper Hop 3×3 Summary (predicted)\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"Eval mean\", \"NVE>1.5× rate\", \"Collapse rate\", \"Baseline%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Baseline\", \"222.6\", \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"100%\"]\n          - [\"CIVO trigger\", \"66.9\", \"3/3\", \"2/3\", \"30.1%\"]\n          - [\"No dt_emb\", \"71.6\", \"0/3\", \"0/3\", \"32.2%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cross-environment summary: 4-5 environments × 3 configs heat map\"\n    analysis: >\n      P2 但若完成则为论文最强 generalization evidence。\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: >\n      P1 探索性实验: RSSM 预测不确定性超过阈值时截断 imagination rollout。\n      Walker Walk, dt=2, 1 seed。全部为预测数据。\n    expected_results:\n      eval_105K_predicted: 485.3\n      nve_peak_predicted: 1.42\n      nve_105K_predicted: 0.73\n      collapse_predicted: false\n      civo_prevented_predicted: true\n      vs_baseline_predicted: \"53.0%\"\n      effective_horizon_mean_predicted: 9.2\n      effective_horizon_std_predicted: 3.4\n      truncation_trigger_rate_predicted: \"38% of rollout steps\"\n      value_calibration_predicted: \"moderate underestimation (NVE 0.6-0.8×)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, uncertainty-gated truncation 是 Intervention Hierarchy 的潜在第四层\n      (Model-based gating)。预测它部分有效: NVE 保持 <1.5× (CIVO technically prevented),\n      但 eval 仅 53% baseline (truncation 过于激进, 缩短了有效 imagination horizon)。\n      这类似于 TCN 的困境: 足以阻止 CIVO 的干预强度也损害了学习。\n      Truncation rate 38% 表明 RSSM 在相当多的 rollout steps 上不确定——这本身\n      就是 RSSM fidelity gap 的直接度量。\n      审稿人可能将此视为 \"interesting pilot but needs more investigation\"——P1\n      定位合理, 不会升级为论文核心贡献, 但为 future work 提供了具体方向。\n      如果添加到 Intervention Hierarchy:\n      L4 (Model-based): Uncertainty truncation 1/1 prevents CIVO but 53% eval retention.\n      与 L3 TCN (2/8, 45-91% retention) 互补: 不同机制, 类似 trade-off。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Uncertainty-Gated Truncation Pilot\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"Comparison\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Eval@105K\", \"485.3\", \"53% baseline (vs TCN σ=0.2 68%)\"]\n          - [\"NVE_peak\", \"1.42\", \"Below 1.5× threshold\"]\n          - [\"Mean effective horizon\", \"9.2/15\", \"Truncation reduces useful imagination\"]\n          - [\"Truncation trigger rate\", \"38%\", \"RSSM uncertain at 38% of steps\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Effective horizon over training + NVE trajectory, showing truncation → NVE suppression\"\n    analysis: >\n      Pilot 结果支持 \"CIVO prevention ↔ learning quality trade-off\" 的系统性发现。\n      可选添加到 Intervention Hierarchy 作为 L4, 但非论文核心。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Aggregate: Cross-Experiment Synthesis Tables\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Aggregate: Intervention Hierarchy Final Table\"\n    plan_id: \"aggregate_intervention_hierarchy\"\n    description: >\n      论文核心 Table: 所有干预方法的系统性评估汇总。整合 C7 + C8 全部数据。\n    expected_results:\n      total_seeds_tested: 42\n      total_methods: 8\n      total_levels: 3\n      total_environments: 3\n      overall_CIVO_prevention_rate: \"4/36 (11.1%) — excluding embedding removal control\"\n      embedding_removal_rate: \"8/8 (100%) — removes the feature entirely\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, Intervention Hierarchy 被认可为系统性贡献。审稿人看到的是:\n      8 种方法, 3 个干预层级, 3 个环境, 42 seeds——这是该类问题的首次系统性评估。\n      关键 narrative: 论文不是 \"我们试了一个方法失败了\", 而是 \"我们系统性地探索了\n      整个干预空间, 发现 CIVO fundamentally hard to mitigate through post-hoc interventions\"。\n      Gradient level (L1) 失败因为 forward-pass damage 不可逆;\n      Output level (L2) 失败因为 EMA anchor 被污染;\n      Representation level (L3) 在最优条件下偶尔成功但不可靠。\n      唯一 100% 有效的方法是移除 feature 本身——这不是 intervention, 是 surrender。\n      这为 future work 提供了明确方向: 需要 architectural solutions (THICK/Hieros\n      式分层时间抽象), 而非 post-hoc patches。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table (论文核心): Intervention Hierarchy\"\n        columns: [\"Level\", \"Method\", \"Success rate\", \"Best eval retention\", \"Primary failure mechanism\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"L1 Gradient\", \"Full SGS\", \"0/3\", \"49%\", \"Forward-pass damage irreducible\"]\n          - [\"L1 Gradient\", \"Obs-decoder SGS\", \"1/6\", \"79% (but critic destroyed)\", \"Compensatory amplification\"]\n          - [\"L1 Gradient\", \"Reward SGS\", \"0/2\", \"36%\", \"No-op (gradient ≠ causality)\"]\n          - [\"L2 Output\", \"RAVE ceil=2.0\", \"0/1\", \"3%\", \"EMA anchor pollution\"]\n          - [\"L2 Output\", \"RAVE ceil=1.5\", \"0/1\", \"8%\", \"EMA anchor pollution\"]\n          - [\"L3 Representation\", \"TCN σ=0.2\", \"2/8*\", \"91%/45% (high variance)\", \"Dose insufficient in complex envs\"]\n          - [\"L3 Representation\", \"TCN σ=0.5\", \"0/3\", \"40%\", \"Overdose (Walker) / Underdose (Cheetah)\"]\n          - [\"L3 Representation\", \"TCN σ=1.0\", \"1/1†\", \"27%\", \"Learning destroyed by noise\"]\n          - [\"**Control**\", \"**dt_emb removal**\", \"**8/8**\", \"**15-37%**\", \"**(removes feature)**\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure: Intervention Hierarchy pyramid visualization with success rates\"\n      - \"* 2/8 includes Walker-only σ=0.2 success; cross-env 0/4\"\n      - \"† Cheetah σ=1.0: technically prevents CIVO (NVE<0.21) but eval 27% → noise destroys learning\"\n    analysis: >\n      论文最重要的 contribution table。Best 档审稿人将此视为 \"systematic negative\n      results that save the community significant wasted effort\"。\n\n  - name: \"Aggregate: NVE Cross-Environment Classification\"\n    plan_id: \"aggregate_nve_classification\"\n    description: >\n      NVE≥1.5× 诊断标记跨环境汇总。\n    expected_results:\n      walker_trained_above_1.5x: \"5/5 (008d s0-s4)\"\n      walker_untrained_above_1.5x: \"0/7 (008f s0-s4 + 008a s0-s2)\"\n      cheetah_trained_above_1.5x: \"3/3 (010b s0-s1 + predicted s2)\"\n      cheetah_untrained_above_1.5x: \"0/5 (024b s0-s1 + 008a_cheetah s0-s1 + predicted)\"\n      pickcube_trained_above_1.5x: \"1/1 (019b)\"\n      pickcube_untrained_above_1.5x: \"0/0 (no control run)\"\n      total_AUROC: 0.969\n      total_sensitivity: 0.93\n      total_specificity: 0.97\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下, NVE 跨环境分类汇总是论文 C2 的 capstone evidence。\n      Trained dt_emb → NVE>1.5× 在 9/9+ 个 independent observations 中成立\n      (部分 seeds 共享 seed number, 需去重)。Untrained → 0/12+ 超过 1.5×。\n      AUROC 0.969 在 4 环境 29 data points 上成立, 尽管是 in-sample。\n      审稿人接受 NVE≥1.5× 作为 \"reliable early-warning diagnostic for CIVO risk\n      in temporal-abstraction world-model RL\", 建议 held-out validation 作为 future work。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: NVE Cross-Environment Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Environment\", \"Trained dt_emb NVE>1.5×\", \"Untrained NVE>1.5×\", \"Max NVE (trained)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", \"5/5\", \"0/7\", \"4.12×\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", \"3/3\", \"0/5\", \"70.64×\"]\n          - [\"PickCube\", \"1/1\", \"—\", \"3.78×\"]\n          - [\"**Total**\", \"**9/9**\", \"**0/12**\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plot: NVE distributions by condition (trained vs untrained) across environments\"\n    analysis: >\n      NVE 诊断方法的 cross-environment robustness confirmation。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"68097478-cbd2-4644-b420-2113bd7d1c88","total_cost_usd":1.51460325,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":78937,"cache_read_input_tokens":339204,"output_tokens":31973,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":78937,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":19802,"cache_read_input_tokens":90026,"cache_creation_input_tokens":752,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_i